: 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dc99586-689f-57dc-a397-af7b36891529', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dc99586-689f-57dc-a397-af7b36891529'}, {'abstract': 'She thinks a single-payer health care system can save more than other analysts think. Here’s where she says she’ll get the money to pay for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/01/upshot/elizabeth-warrens-medicare-for-all-math.html', 'snippet': 'She thinks a single-payer health care system can save more than other analysts think. Here’s where she says she’ll get the money to pay for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Warren’s “Medicare for all” proposal would make substantial shifts to how the United States pays for its health care system. She would eliminate most other forms of coverage, including private insurance, and provide all Americans with a generous government-run plan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/upshot/up-warren-explain/merlin_163676349_f1659fc6-5619-4e15-85aa-f6e95c5bb850-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/01/upshot/up-warren-explain/merlin_163676349_f1659fc6-5619-4e15-85aa-f6e95c5bb850-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/upshot/up-warren-explain/merlin_163676349_f1659fc6-5619-4e15-85aa-f6e95c5bb850-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo