 the techniques he used to help locate sunken submarines and enormous stone heads, as well as early applications for artificial intelligence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/01/science/sheldon-breiner-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He developed the techniques he used to help locate sunken submarines and enormous stone heads, as well as early applications for artificial intelligence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the compass was invented, perhaps about 2,000 years ago, humans have used Earth’s magnetic field to guide them. Many ages later, Sheldon Breiner devised ways to use magnetism to guide him to things that might otherwise never have been found — like sunken ships, a lost city and colossal basalt heads buried underground.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/obituaries/07breiner-print2/31breiner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/07/obituaries/07breiner-print2/31breiner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 495}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/obituaries/07breiner-print2/31breiner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/obituaries/07breiner-print2/31breiner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1691, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/obituaries/07breiner-print2/31breiner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb