en there’s the act of ironing. The satisfaction of seeing cotton, silk, linen and even denim smooth out and straighten gives me a kind of strange, existential high. I approach these chores like a spiritual discipline, on par with fasting and prayer. There’s something about the careful consideration required to do them well that puts me at ease.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 615}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1998, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/03vidal/03vidal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Love Housework. Let Me Explain.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pleasure of Household Chores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orderliness and Clutter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irons and Ironing Boards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-02T18:03:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juan Vidal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vidal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a707c5c2-9db7-56db-a8af-9827c0b888e4', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a707c5c2-9db7-56db-a8af-9827c0b888e4'}, {'abstract': 'Forget Scandinavia. Switzerland is richer and yet has a surprisingly equal wealth distribution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/02/opinion/sunday/switzerland-capitalism-wealth.html', 'snippet': 'Forget Scandinavia. Switzerland is richer and yet has a surprisingly equal wealth distribution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many progressive intellectuals, Bernie Sanders traces his vision of economic paradise not to socialist dictatorships like Venezuela but to their distant cousins in Scandinavia, which are just as wealthy and democratic as the United States but have more equitable distributions of wealth, as well as affordable health care and free college for all.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/sunday/03sharma/03sharma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/opinion/sunday/03sharma/03sharma-articleLa