me': 'persons', 'value': 'Conway, Kellyanne', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-03T19:16:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catie Edmondson and Nicholas Fandos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edmondson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c86123c0-940c-5423-bbc1-c5713d0b4616', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c86123c0-940c-5423-bbc1-c5713d0b4616'}, {'abstract': 'Being arrested at her age has its hazards, like keeping balanced with bound hands. But the star says she feels the need to do more about climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/03/arts/television/04jane-fonda-arrest-protest.html', 'snippet': 'Being arrested at her age has its hazards, like keeping balanced with bound hands. But the star says she feels the need to do more about climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The night before Jane Fonda was arrested here again last week, a member of her social media team asked whether she would consider writing a letter from jail. “With what?” Fonda replied. “I’ll be without my phone.” She paused a beat, “Or adult diapers.” Also, Fonda continued, musing out loud, it was one thing for the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. to write a letter from jail. But her? The plan was nixed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04jane-fonda-01/merlin_163683525_58b8ec73-ecd6-4a40-a256-c05af00390df-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, '