nese-Americans during World War II — and serves as a warning today for our own fractured society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT WAS THE LATE ’60s, and a University of California, Berkeley, undergraduate named Shawn Wong wanted to write the next great American novel. He was born in Oakland, Calif., in 1949 to parents who emigrated from Tianjin, China, both of whom died by the time he was 15. Wong had fallen in love with literature, enchanted by James Joyce, Samuel Beckett and William Carlos Williams, and he, too, wanted to embark on a life as a writer.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '43', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/t-magazine/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/17/t-magazine/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/t-magazine/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/t-magazine/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1134, 'width': 1685, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/t-magazine/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/17/t-magazine/17tmag-nonoboy-slide-6XRL/17tm