paragraph': 'A progressive organization is plunging itself into the presidential campaign, unveiling plans to spend $75 million on digital advertising to counter President Trump’s early spending advantage in key 2020 battleground states.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/merlin_163681221_541bfb66-90be-4338-82e0-826efb6ac901-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/merlin_163681221_541bfb66-90be-4338-82e0-826efb6ac901-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/merlin_163681221_541bfb66-90be-4338-82e0-826efb6ac901-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/merlin_163681221_541bfb66-90be-4338-82e0-826efb6ac901-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/00-demdigitalgroup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/00-demdigitalgroup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/us/politics/00-demdigitalgroup1/00-demdigitalgroup1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democratic Strategists Set Up $75 Million Digital Campaign to Counter Trump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democratic Strategists Prepare $75 Million Digital Ad Campaign to Counter Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-04T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shane Goldmacher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldmacher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79ac9ff7-9137-50cc-a7be-b19767879b0f', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79ac9ff7-9137-50cc-a7be-b19767879b0f'}, {'abstract': 'She has led the way, but all the candidates need to come clean about their health care proposals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/04/opinion/warren-medicare-for-all.html', 'snippet': 'She has led the way, but all the candidates need to come clean about their health care proposals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laying the table for the next Democratic debate, Elizabeth Warren has issued a plan that explains how she would fund what she calls Medicare for All. She had studiously avoided saying whether it would raise taxes for the middle class, and in her proposal, she says (repeatedly) it will not. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04rosenthalWeb/04rosenthalWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elizabeth Warren Throws Down the Gauntlet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-04T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3283a7b-7aa3-5df6-adfb-a6e66fa812b1', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3283a7b-7aa3-5df6-adfb-a6e66fa812b1'}, {'abstract': 'And without reform, neither is a Democratic Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/04/opinion/warren-sanders-filibuster.html', 'snippet': 'And without reform, neither is a Democratic Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are still more than a dozen candidates jockeying for the Democratic presidential nomination. Some are running on big, ambitious platforms for change, like the Medicare-for-All plans pushed by Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren. Others are selling “pragmatism,” with more modest ideas meant to win consensus — and which are often quite liberal by historical standards. But nearly everyone on the board faces the same, fundamental problem: They want to go further than where Congress, and the Senate in particular, will want to move, even if it has a Democratic majority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04Bouie-1/04Bouie-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 489, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04Bouie-1/04Bouie-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 489}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/opinion/04Bouie-1/04Bouie-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/o