 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-04T17:35:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manuela Andreoni and Letícia Casado', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manuela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andreoni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Letícia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8025d717-e475-5961-9a3d-0ca5503c3dac', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8025d717-e475-5961-9a3d-0ca5503c3dac'}, {'abstract': 'The Puerto Rican astrologer, who died Saturday, left behind a cultural legacy in all of Latin America, where for decades many followed his predictions with devotion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/04/arts/walter-mercado-tribute.html', 'snippet': 'The Puerto Rican astrologer, who died Saturday, left behind a cultural legacy in all of Latin America, where for decades many followed his predictions with devotion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since I can remember, Walter Mercado was a part of my life and a presence in our household. He was on television shows and radio segments, his smiling photo accompanying the horoscope section of magazines and daily newspapers. “Check Walter’s horoscope” was the answer to many an existential concern. For millions of people in Latin America, the day could not begin without reading or listening to Walter’s predictions. Growing up in Aibonito, a small town surrounded by mountains in the center of Puerto Rico, I was sure that he had a direct line to the stars, and that his job was to translate their wisdom to us. Walter, who died Nov. 2, knew things that we didn’t.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/merlin_163850496_87b6006c-8260-4d6b-a91f-e38bb26c385f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/merlin_163850496_87b6006c-8260-4d6b-a91f-e38bb26c385f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/merlin_163850496_87b6006c-8260-4d6b-a91f-e38bb26c385f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/merlin_163850496_87b6006c-8260-4d6b-a91f-e38bb26c385f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/04Mercado-Tribute01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/04Mercado-Tribute01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/arts/04Mercado-Tribute01/04Mercado-Tribute01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Walter Mercado: There Was a Duality to Everything About Him', 'kicker': 'An Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_h