, Donald J', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parnas, Lev', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shokin, Viktor', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burisma Holdings Ltd', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Hunter', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-04T20:50:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d5d95d3-8f98-5adc-bc24-473155d86468', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d5d95d3-8f98-5adc-bc24-473155d86468'}, {'abstract': 'This fish, raised in Pacific waters off Baja California, makes a worthy substitute for wild striped bass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/04/dining/pacifico-striped-bass.html', 'snippet': 'This fish, raised in Pacific waters off Baja California, makes a worthy substitute for wild striped bass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wild striped bass, also called stripers or rockfish, are a treasure. Nothing quite compares with the sleek, muscular fish. Until now, farmed versions have been a hybrid with little flavor or succulence. But a new kind of farmed striped bass has come on the market that’s not a hybrid; it is genuine Morone saxatilis, the same as the wild fish. They are being raised in deep waters of the Pacific off northern Baja California. The company, Pacifico, says it has an agreement with the Mexican government for the only aquafarm in that area, a marine sanctuary with no industry nearby. The fish are raised on feed made mostly from the trimmings of other fish. I roasted a one-and-a-half pounder, cleaned and scaled but whole, with a fillet of wild striped bass alongside to compare them. The thick flesh of the wild fillet, from a big fish, was firm yet silky; the texture of the farmed fish was less firm. As for the flavor, they were similar, though the farmed fish was not as rich.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/dining/04burner1/04burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Farmed Striped Bass Worth Roasting', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cook: Farmed Striped Bass That’s Worth Roasting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bass (Fish)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baja California (Mexico)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whole Foods Market Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacifico Aquaculture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-04T20:52:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/894539bb-04aa-509f-b427-b549f486f259', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/894539bb-04aa-509f-b427-b549f486f259'}, {'abstract': 'To mark the end of the era, the pilot on the retirement flight for the 747 in Israel’s national airline zigged and zagged, following a route shaped like the jet itself. Call it sky art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/04/business/el-al-747.html', 'snippet': 'To mark the end of the era, the pilot on the retirement flight for the 747 in Israel’s national airline zigged and zagged, following a route shaped like the jet itself. Call it sky art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not often that an airline draws attention to a late flight, as was the case on Sunday when an El Al jumbo jet from Rome to Tel Aviv landed 95 minutes after it had been scheduled to arrive. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/04/multimedia/04xp-elal/04xp-elal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/04/multimedia/04xp-elal/04xp-elal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xl