/27f912e0-0dc3-5c59-b838-ae4dcb54cc96'}, {'abstract': 'Trump is not the first president to defy Congress. A struggle for power has been playing out since the nation’s founding — as its framers intended.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/magazine/congress-president-impeachment.html', 'snippet': 'Trump is not the first president to defy Congress. A struggle for power has been playing out since the nation’s founding — as its framers intended.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early October, President Trump’s White House counsel, Pat Cipollone, sent a defiant letter to four leaders of the House of Representatives. No one in the Trump administration, Cipollone declared, would participate in the impeachment inquiry that Speaker Nancy Pelosi opened in September after Trump’s phone call with President Volodymyr Zelensky of Ukraine came to light. “Because participating in this inquiry under the current unconstitutional posture would inflict lasting institutional harm on the executive branch and lasting damage to the separation of powers, you have left the president no choice,” Cipollone concluded.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 648}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 949, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1897, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-impunity-01/10mag-impunity-01-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens When a President and Congress Go to War?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Checks and Imbalances', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trump-Ukraine Whistle-blower Complaint and Impeachment Inquiry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiff, Adam B', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5377679-1f19-5678-b6ed-0157c28c553e', 'word_count': 2842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5377679-1f19-5678-b6ed-0157c28c553e'}, {'abstract': 'Listlessness was Juan Carlos Onetti’s great theme. He ushered Spanish-language fiction into modernity and influenced writers from Julio Cortázar to Mario Vargas Llosa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/books/review/juan-carlos-onetti.html', 'snippet': 'Listlessness was Juan Carlos Onetti’s great theme. He ushered Spanish-language fiction into modernity and influenced writers from Julio Cortázar to Mario Vargas Llosa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1974, Juan Carlos Onetti (1909-94), Uruguay’s most distinguished modern writer, and his colleagues at Marcha, a prominent weekly in Montevideo, had a run-in with the dictatorship of Juan María Bordaberry, then in its second year. Their mistake was to award the magazine’s literary prize to a story about a murderous Uruguayan police inspector; when it was published, several staff members were summarily imprisoned. For six weeks Onetti languished in a mental institution. It took a campaign led by international writers — including Onetti’s admirers Gabriel García Márquez and Mario Vargas Llosa — to persuade his jailers to set him free. Soon after his release Onetti moved to Madrid, where he remained until his death, despite a personal visit from Bordaberry’s first democratically elected successor, Julio María Sanguinetti, who flew to Spain in 1985 to present him with the Uruguayan National Literature prize.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/books/review/05Asokan-RovingEye/05Asokan-RovingEye-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South American Literature’s Master of Malaise', 'kicker': 'Roving Eye', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Master of Malaise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uruguay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ONETTI, JUAN CARLOS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Dream Come True (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ratik Asokan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ratik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asokan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87ae6935-98b8-599b-bdb8-4b8f23da6702', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87ae6935-98b8-599b-bdb8-4b8f23da6702'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on reporting a toxic male boss and giving up pets for a grandson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/magazine/what-should-i-do-about-my-awful-sexist-boss.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on reporting a toxic male boss and giving up pets for a grandson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I just finished a big project working under a male manager with whom I don’t get along. (I’m a woman in my 20s, and he’s significantly older.) We work in teams and our members spend a lot of time together — working, traveling, socializing. People who haven’t worked with this manager see him as charismatic and friendly. When he gets stressed, however, he has temper tantrums, snaps at people and digs in to defend his positions, rejecting all opposing points of view. This behavior is unpleasant, especially when it’s directed at me. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/magazine/10mag-ethicist/10mag-ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should I Do About My Awful, Sexist Boss?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Should I Do About My Awful, Sexist Boss?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Hazards and Violations', 'rank'