or': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T10:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Marino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d643051-b771-5b34-866a-cf9a92b89902', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d643051-b771-5b34-866a-cf9a92b89902'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “The Witches Are Coming,” by Lindy West.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/books/review/the-witches-are-coming-by-lindy-west-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “The Witches Are Coming,” by Lindy West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, my husband was at a bar in Chicago. A friend had told him to check out this particular bar because it’s a cool dive run by queer people of color, with dancing and cheap drinks and a good vibe. So he was sitting there, having a beer, and after a while a guy came in and sat down next to him. White guy, late forties. Polo shirt. Mustache probably. Khaki shorts. Standard random white guy. The guy—his name was Larry or Barry or something, so for the purposes of this story let’s call him LarryBarry— struck up a conversation with my husband, asked him if he was having fun. My husband said, “Yeah, this is a fun bar! People are dancing. It’s cool.” And the guy got a real sad look on his face and said, “Yeah, this is one of my favorite songs. I wish I was dancing right now.” So naturally my husband asked, “Well, why don’t you go dance?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Witches Are Coming’ by Lindy West: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T10:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/84bf0cec-abbd-5975-99cf-17317d59c7b2', 'word_count': 2641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84bf0cec-abbd-5975-99cf-17317d59c7b2'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from ‘In the Dream House’ by Carmen Maria Machado', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/books/review/in-the-dream-house-by-carmen-maria-machado-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from ‘In the Dream House’ by Carmen Maria Machado', 'lead_paragraph': 'I never read prologues. I find them tedious. If what the author has to say is so important, why relegate it to the paratext? What are they trying to hide?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘In the Dream House’ by Carmen Maria Machado: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T10:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac59c8f-2fd2-51d3-bbd4-2ea03e743b42', 'word_count': 1730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac59c8f-2fd2-51d3-bbd4-2ea03e743b42'}, {'abstract': 'Start with a breathtaking site in Vermont, then get out the Lego blocks. If you choose the right architects, they’ll understand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/realestate/how-to-build-a-modern-barn.html', 'snippet': 'Start with a breathtaking site in Vermont, then get out the Lego blocks. If you choose the right architects, they’ll understand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years ago, Marc and Lana Reuss found themselves happily untethered, in the enviable position of being able to make a new home for themselves almost anywhere they pleased.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page'