e': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Foundation for the Righteous', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yad Vashem Holocaust Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T14:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Iliana Magra', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Iliana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Magra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4efbd7e-d307-5919-b9f0-1fc47ae5b726', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4efbd7e-d307-5919-b9f0-1fc47ae5b726'}, {'abstract': 'Season 2 of “The End of the ____ing World” starts streaming on Netflix, and a live production of the beloved Disney classic airs on ABC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday-a-dark-coming-of-age-comedy-and-the-little-mermaid-live.html', 'snippet': 'Season 2 of “The End of the ____ing World” starts streaming on Netflix, and a live production of the beloved Disney classic airs on ABC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE END OF THE ____ING WORLD Stream on Netflix. Underneath the morbid premise of this comedy, based on Charles Forsman’s graphic novel, lies a sweet coming-of-age love story between two misfit teenagers who begin to understand themselves better as they wrestle with their feelings for each another. The first season follows the misadventures of Alyssa (Jessica Barden), a high schooler looking for companionship, and James (Alex Lawther), a psychopath who fakes his affection for Alyssa and plans to kill her. Together they steal a car and embark on a violent road trip that doubles as a journey of self-discovery. That is, until the cops catch up to them. Season 2 picks up with Alyssa seeming to have returned to a life of domesticity. The series shares similarities with “Flowers,” another dark British comedy on Netflix that deals with searing adult themes in a way that’s palatably quirky.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/05tvcol-end/05tvcol-end-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday: A Dark Coming of Age Comedy and ‘The Little Mermaid Live!’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 's