e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6a0e498-7a02-5c94-8688-a8f2d01c9082', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6a0e498-7a02-5c94-8688-a8f2d01c9082'}, {'abstract': 'A save-the-date card is not a subpoena. You are allowed to skip being in the bridal party, attending a shower or bachelor/bachelorette party and even the wedding itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/fashion/weddings/how-to-say-no-to-friends-during-wedding-season.html', 'snippet': 'A save-the-date card is not a subpoena. You are allowed to skip being in the bridal party, attending a shower or bachelor/bachelorette party and even the wedding itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Search for “bridesmaid proposal” on Etsy and you’ll be met with 49,465 results. There are the cutesy mugs (“I can’t marry my mister without my sister”) and the cards that seem less of a request than an order (“You’re obviously going to be my maid of honor — and no, that wasn’t a question”). These 49,465 data points perfectly illustrate why so many people feel like they can’t say no to being in a bridal party, or to any of the other social contracts associated with modern weddings.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/fashion/00HOWTOSAYNOart/00HOWTOSAYNOart-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/fashion/00HOWTOSAYNOart/00HOWTOSAYNOart-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/fashion/00HOWTOSAYNOart/00HOWTOSAYNOart-jumbo.gif', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo',