ign', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b302f8-ac2d-561f-b6e7-df7dceba8c0d', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b302f8-ac2d-561f-b6e7-df7dceba8c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/style/tiny-modern-love-stories-i-couldnt-breathe-or-cancel.html', 'snippet': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a child, I hated my schizophrenic mother’s too-big body. As a young woman, I starved myself, only learning to eat at 26, after my mother overdosed on her medication and died. Still, I recoiled from cameras, fearful that photos would reveal that I, too, was fat. At 38, I found a letter she’d sent me at camp: “It’s so lonely without you. I love + miss you A LOT.” I wept. That night, my fiancée, Shannon, took my picture. Studying my breasts, stomach, thighs, I saw my mother. “I love you, too,” I said, silently, as if in prayer. — Leanne Milech', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/fashion/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5/00OCT-ML-TINY-LOVE-ILLO5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Love Stories: ‘I Couldn’t Breathe — or Cancel’', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-05T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d752ea7-51d1-57c7-a537-663e93d27249', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d752ea7-51d1-57c7-a537-663e93d27249'}, {'abstract': 'All around the world, protesters wear Guy Fawkes masks to conceal their identity in service of a cause.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/05/opinion/guy-fawkes-day-v-for-vendetta.html', 'snippet': 'All around the world, protesters wear Guy Fawkes masks to conceal their identity in service of a cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lately it seems like everyone has something to protest. The streets are filled with the noise of dissent, from marchers demanding democracy in Hong Kong to demonstrators insisting on economic equality in Chile to climate activists chanting worldwide. Oddly, wherever they take place and whatever their particular grievance, these movements all claim a failed 17th-century British insurgent as their symbolic confederate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/opinion/00guy12/merlin_162227496_a17195ad-c3f1-4717-8446-d4c42e4d43b0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/30/opinion/00guy12/merlin_162227496_a17195ad-c3f1-4717-8446-d4c42e4d43b0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/opinion/00guy12/merlin_162227496_a17195ad-c3f1-4717-8446-d4c42e4d43b0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/opinion/00guy12/merlin_162227496_a17195ad-c3f1-4717-8446-d4c42e4d43b0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1327, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/opinion/00guy12/merlin_162227496_a17195ad-c3f1-4717-8446-d4c42e4d43b0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 's