 'Six months after King Maha Vajiralongkorn’s coronation, aide after aide has been ousted and denounced, even as he moves to bolster his authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — The denunciations have swirled through Thailand’s gilded palaces with the rhetorical extravagance of a Shakespearean history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/merlin_163072821_9f6b0c57-8a31-4bc6-8be7-ce092d0b52c0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/merlin_163072821_9f6b0c57-8a31-4bc6-8be7-ce092d0b52c0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/merlin_163072821_9f6b0c57-8a31-4bc6-8be7-ce092d0b52c0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/merlin_163072821_9f6b0c57-8a31-4bc6-8be7-ce092d0b52c0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/00thailand-king-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/00thailand-king-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/01/world/00thailand-king-4/00thailand-king-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Extremely Evil Misconduct’: Thailand’s Palace Intrigue Spills Into View', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Purging Palace of ‘Evil,’ Thai King Bolsters Rule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vajiralongkorn (1952- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhumibol Adulyadej', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sineenat Wongvajirapakdi (1985- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suthida Vajiralongkorn Na Ayudhya (1978- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ubolratana  (1951- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Srirasmi Suwadee (1971- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-06T05:29:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Beech', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beech', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43b16874-af84-5981-8847-6961440d0993', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43b16874-af84-5981-8847-6961440d0993'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary about the Apollo Theater airs on HBO. And AMC offers a pair of Martin Scorsese gangster movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/06/arts/television/whats-on-tv-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary about the Apollo Theater airs on HBO. And AMC offers a pair of Martin Scorsese gangster movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE APOLLO (2019) 9 p.m. on HBO. “When you walk out of the wings and you take the mic,” the Harlem figure Lana Turner says in this documentary, “you have stood on top of the music scores, the gag lines, the costumes, the singers. You’ve stood on top of all of them. And their spirit — and their souls — are in that floor.” She’s talking about the Apollo Theater in Harlem, the venerated launching pad of several generations of musicians, comics and other performers. Directed by Roger Ross Williams, “The Apollo” digs into the theater’s rich, 85-year history through a trove of archival performance footage (Billie Holiday, Ray Charles, Aretha Franklin and James Brown are among those featured) and recent interviews, which it intersperses with scenes of the preparation and performance of a stage version of Ta-Nehisi Coates’s “Between the World and Me” that debuted last year. The results are “conventional but entertaining,” Ben Kenigsberg wrote in his review for The New York Times. “While ‘The Apollo’ itself might have taken a more inventive approach,” he added, “it derives its power from the artistry it captures.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06tvcol-theapollo/06tvcol-theapollo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06tvcol-theapollo/06tvcol-theapollo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06tvcol-theapollo/06tvcol-theapollo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i