x Cuts and Jobs Act (2017)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Zones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clyburn, James E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kind, Ron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milken, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mnuchin, Steven T', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neal, Richard E', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Black Caucus', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-06T14:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton and Jesse Drucker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drucker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c886c65-0dac-5290-810d-0dd499534fd8', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c886c65-0dac-5290-810d-0dd499534fd8'}, {'abstract': 'Leonardo’s painting is a security hazard, an educational obstacle and not even a satisfying bucket-list item. It’s time the Louvre moved it out of the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/06/arts/design/mona-lisa-louvre-overcrowding.html', 'snippet': 'Leonardo’s painting is a security hazard, an educational obstacle and not even a satisfying bucket-list item. It’s time the Louvre moved it out of the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Even in a city saturated with excellent fall exhibitions, from the Grand Palais’s retrospective of El Greco to the Fondation Louis Vuitton’s showcase of Charlotte Perriand, the show of the season here is the decade-in-the-works “Leonardo da Vinci,” at the Musée du Louvre. Mandatory timed tickets are sold out through November for this thorough, deeply serious exhibition, which sloughs off the myths that cling to this least productive of Renaissance masters. You will find here a cleaner, sprightlier Leonardo — or at least you will in the show downstairs, where four of the Louvre’s five paintings by the artist have been relocated.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06leonardo-notebook1-promo/06leonardo-notebook1-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06leonardo-notebook1-promo/06leonardo-notebook1-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06leonardo-notebook1-promo/06leonardo-notebook1-promo-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06leonardo-notebook1-promo/06leonardo-notebook1-promo-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06leonardo-notebook1-promo/06leonardo-notebook1-promo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/06/arts/06leonardo-notebook1-promo/06leonardo-notebook1-promo-thu