alifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c34a4b2b-8732-56d4-bdbf-aefedc640e2b', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c34a4b2b-8732-56d4-bdbf-aefedc640e2b'}, {'abstract': 'Demagogues like Hungary’s Viktor Orban denounce the European Union but corruptly exploit its farm subsidies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/06/opinion/eu-hungary-farm-subsidies.html', 'snippet': 'Demagogues like Hungary’s Viktor Orban denounce the European Union but corruptly exploit its farm subsidies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is galling is how openly Prime Minister Viktor Orban does it, blaming the European Union for every imagined indignity or interference in Hungary’s affairs, while milking billions from Brussels to enrich his cronies and prop up his illiberal rule. He is not alone, as a Times investigation of the bloc’s lavish farm subsidies demonstrates in shocking detail — the governments of several formerly Communist Eastern European states have also cynically taken advantage of the union’s largess through opaque deals, feeding a new class of land barons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/opinion/06farm/06farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/06/opinion/06farm/06farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/opinion/06farm/06farm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/opinion/06farm/06farm-superJ