pes of numerous TV and movie police procedurals.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Crown Vic” begins in the midst of a kinetic shootout, the camera zipping back and forth as a pair of masked robbers careen away from the L.A.P.D. in a car. But the writer-director Joel Souza soon dissipates the adrenaline rush of this opening into a verbose, hackneyed thriller about a night in the lives of a veteran patrol officer and his trainee.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/05/arts/crownvic1/crownvic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Crown Vic’ Review: A Cop Thriller Abounding in Cliché', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crown Vic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Crown Vic (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Souza, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kleintank, Luke (1990- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jane, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-07T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Devika Girish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Devika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Girish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/459b0244-daec-5e0c-a232-4f6bf50cf185', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/459b0244-daec-5e0c-a232-4f6bf50cf185'}, {'abstract': 'In a film he wrote, the actor plays a version of his own father. Too bad the bullying character based on LaBeouf has little desire for introspection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/07/movies/honey-boy-review.html', 'snippet': 'In a film he wrote, the actor plays a version of his own father. Too bad the bullying character based on LaBeouf has little desire for introspection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the talented actor Shia LaBeouf, who started in film and television as a child, has been acting out his emotional disturbances and drug and alcohol issues in public. In the wake of a 2017 arrest during which he made racist remarks, he has been taking more sober stock of his life and art. He wrote the screenplay and plays a major role in “Honey Boy,” directed by Alma Har’el in her fiction feature debut.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mu