man and a good-time American living in Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'British novelists do love their aptonyms. Dickens had Scrooge (and dozens of others), Martin Amis had Mary Lamb, and for her first novel, “The Earthquake Bird,” Susanna Jones had Lucy Fly. Lucy, for reasons illuminated in the unfolding of a missing-person mystery, zoomed from England to Japan as soon as she was legally able. But even in her new home she seems caged and eager to take wing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/arts/07earthquake/merlin_163598550_844be8c4-bd6b-4f89-be24-db6ead396b32-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 249, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/08/arts/07earthquake/merlin_163598550_844be8c4-bd6b-4f89-be24-db6ead396b32-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 249}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/arts/07earthquake/merlin_163598550_844be8c4-bd6b-4f89-be24-db6ead396b32-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/arts/07earthquake/merlin_163598550_844be8c4-bd6b-4f89-be24-db6ead396b32-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/arts/07earthquake/07earthquake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/08/arts/07earthquake/07earthquake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge