“Strange Birds,” four girls are determined to stop a scout tradition involving real birds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/07/books/review/strange-birds-celia-perez.html', 'snippet': 'In Celia C. Pérez’s “Strange Birds,” four girls are determined to stop a scout tradition involving real birds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We hear so much about the challenges of young female friendships. But STRANGE BIRDS: A Field Guide to Ruffling Feathers (Kokila, 350 pp., $16.99; ages 8 to 12), Celia C. Pérez’s second middle-grade novel (after “The First Rule of Punk”), is a story about the magic and beauty of these bonds, especially when they are created through commitments to something greater. We meet four girls who live in the fictional town of Sabal Palms, Fla. — girls who are beginning to learn about the world and forge their identities. But how do you do that in a place where you don’t feel encouraged to be yourself?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10-BKS-SANCHEZ/10-BKS-SANCHEZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10-BKS-SANCHEZ/10-BKS-SANCHEZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 858}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10-BKS-SANCHEZ/10-BKS-SANCHEZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 717, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10-BKS-SANCHEZ/10-BKS-SANCHEZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1433, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 