view/picture-books-maya-angelou-august-wilson-ruth-asawa.html', 'snippet': 'New picture books about creators including Ruth Asawa, Maya Angelou and August Wilson let children get to know the real-life people behind great works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Works of art engage our hearts and excite our imaginations, but often the creators behind the work remain a mystery. Lately, however, picture books have taken up that cause, giving children a chance to look into artists’ lives and begin to get to know their work. These new books about American artists and writers include some familiar names like Maya Angelou and William Carlos Williams. Others are less well known, like Ruth Asawa and Tyrus Wong. This diverse mix of makers have life stories that take us from coast to coast, and open doors and windows to the larger world. Best of all, each book offers insight and inspiration to young readers — and young creators — through dynamic, original art and great writing.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10Crews-1/10Crews-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10Crews-1/10Crews-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10Crews-1/10Crews-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/books/review/10Crews-1/10Crews-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 