 treated humanely as the company prepares to lay off thousands of people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/08/business/wework-employee-letter.html', 'snippet': 'More than 150 employees of WeWork sent a letter to management this week asking to be treated humanely as the company prepares to lay off thousands of people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 150 employees of WeWork sent a letter to management this week asking to be treated humanely as the company prepares to lay off thousands of people. The employees, who call themselves the WeWorkers Coalition, made clear their anger at the company’s co-founder and former chief executive, Adam Neumann, and implored WeWork’s leaders to treat them with “dignity.” Here’s what the letter said: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 962, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 962, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/business/08wework-letter1/08wework-letter1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Are Not the Adam Neumanns of This World’: What WeWork Employees Told Their Bosses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WeWork Companies Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neumann, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-08T10:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bfbed5d-4b8c-5de6-b427-7c0fb554b419', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bfbed5d-4b8c-5de6-b427-7c0fb554b419'}, {'abstract': 'Why a movement that claims to support the American descendants of slavery is being promoted by conservatives and attacked on the left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/08/us/slavery-black-immigrants-ados.html', 'snippet': 'Why a movement that claims to support the American descendants of slavery is being promoted by conservatives and attacked on the left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Hollywood, Harriet Tubman is played in a new movie by a black British woman, much to the annoyance of some black Americans. On the United States census, an ultrawealthy Nigerian immigrant and a struggling African-American woman from the South are expected to check the same box. When many American universities tout their diversity numbers, black students who were born in the Bronx and the Bahamas are counted as the same. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/merlin_162387804_3bb636ab-352e-454e-aa26-ec0b99584639-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/merlin_162387804_3bb636ab-352e-454e-aa26-ec0b99584639-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/merlin_162387804_3bb636ab-352e-454e-aa26-ec0b99584639-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/merlin_162387804_3bb636ab-352e-454e-aa26-ec0b99584639-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/00ados-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/00ados-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/07/us/00ados-01/00ados-01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘We’re Self-Interested’: The Growing Identity Debate in Black America', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Debate Over Black Identity And Ancestral Links to Slavery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Descendants of Slavery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MOORE, ANTONIO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carnell, Yvette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-08T10:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farah Stockman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stockman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/778928fd-ae33-5685-b5b5-7aea0fd3ab82', 'word_count': 1832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/778928fd-ae33-5685-b5b5-7aea0fd3ab82'}, {'abstract': 'Approval of a fossil-fuel plant was overturned after opponents were shut out of a meeting. Now the city has a new chance to consider energy economics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/08/business/energy-environment/gas-power-plants.html', 'snippet': 'Approval of a fossil-fuel plant was overturned after opponents were shut out of a meeting. Now the city has a new chance to consider energy economics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Susan Guidry stepped up as a volunteer in New Orleans after Hurricane Katrina, helping clear debris from the streets as part of a group calling itself the Katrina Krewe. She saw firsthand the disaster’s toll, including the crippling of the power supply. When voters elected her to the City Council, she said, she hardly knew what a kilowatt was. But she came to the conclusion that the city had to change its approach to energy.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/business/00gasplant1/merlin_159860808_0641f8fa-3a53-4928-a68f-d722b85284f6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline'