0/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday-back-to-life-rick-and-morty.html', 'snippet': 'Daisy Haggard’s dark comedy about second chances hits Showtime, and “Rick & Morty” returns after a two-year hiatus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BACK TO LIFE 10 p.m. on Showtime. When Miri Matteson (Daisy Haggard) re-emerges in her isolated seaside hometown after spending 18 years in prison for a violent crime, it’s her secretive past, and that of those around her, that come to the fore. Across the new show’s six episodes, it becomes clear that “the people she’s closest to, including her mother, Caroline (Geraldine James), her former best friend, Mandy (Christine Bottomley), and the affable new neighbor, Billy (Adeel Akhtar), are harboring secrets that start to make her own past transgression look tolerable,” Mike Hale writes in his New York Times review. This series, which Haggard created and helped write, has already drawn comparisons to “Fleabag” — another female-led British show that shares the executive producers Harry and Jack Williams and has a similar focus on dark humor, grief and redemption. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10tvcol-back/10tvcol-back-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10tvcol-back/10tvcol-back-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10tvcol-back/10tvcol-back-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10tvcol-back/10tvcol-back-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'su