ass-metropolitan-opera.html', 'snippet': 'A 1984 work has its premiere at the Metropolitan Opera in a spellbinding production, starring Anthony Roth Costanzo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of Philip Glass’s many, many operas — 30 or so, depending on how you count — “Akhnaten” may be the most ritualistic and mystical. With the subdued, undulating opening of the long orchestral prelude, Mr. Glass is sending a message: Put aside your typical expectations of music drama. This isn’t “Tosca”; you’re on Glass time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10metopera1/merlin_163969761_1c758ac1-7089-4e50-aa43-c2e40c2a9105-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10metopera1/merlin_163969761_1c758ac1-7089-4e50-aa43-c2e40c2a9105-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10metopera1/merlin_163969761_1c758ac1-7089-4e50-aa43-c2e40c2a9105-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10metopera1/merlin_163969761_1c758ac1-7089-4e50-aa43-c2e40c2a9105-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1565, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10metopera1/10metopera1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/10/arts/10metopera1/10metopera1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75