feel like a mournful time, but there are pleasures in its gray solitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — To walk in any well-managed forest during November is to confront the inevitability of death.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1385, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/11/opinion/11renklWeb/11renklWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ode to a Dark Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autumn (Season)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-11T12:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Renkl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Renkl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f925a842-6b75-52b5-921e-3775671235de', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f925a842-6b75-52b5-921e-3775671235de'}, {'abstract': 'There is a lot to learn from mistakes that the Continent’s regulators have made, say consumer groups, lawyers and rival companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/11/business/europe-technology-antitrust-regulation.html', 'snippet': 'There is a lot to learn from mistakes that the Continent’s regulators have made, say consumer groups, lawyers and rival companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Richard Stables should have felt vindicated when the European Union announced a $2.7 billion fine in 2017 against Google for breaking antitrust laws. He had raised alarms about the search giant’s power for years. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/business/00eulessons1/merlin_163837752_a4dd6a2d-984a-478d-8b97-8a606e65fc9c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/06/business/00eulessons1/merlin_163837752_a4dd6a2d-984a-478d-8b97-8a606e65fc9c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/06/business/00eulessons1/merlin_163837752_a4dd6a