 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-11T12:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Satariano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Satariano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc124ae-f07a-519d-b46b-6c4acb86f989', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc124ae-f07a-519d-b46b-6c4acb86f989'}, {'abstract': 'Bloomberg, Dimon and Gates call liberal tax ideas unfair. But excessive wealth is the real threat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/11/opinion/billionaires-warren-wealth-tax.html', 'snippet': 'Bloomberg, Dimon and Gates call liberal tax ideas unfair. But excessive wealth is the real threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The billionaire class has begun unloading on Elizabeth Warren. A few days ago, Jamie Dimon of JPMorgan Chase — at just $1.6 billion in net worth, a comparative piker — said Senator Warren “vilifies successful people.” Then Bill Gates ($107 billion), in an onstage interview with The Times’s Andrew Ross Sorkin, mused about what his tax bill might be in a Warren presidency and left the door open to voting for Donald Trump should Democrats nominate Ms. Warren. And then Michael Bloomberg ($52 billion), who had previously criticized Ms. Warren as anti-corporate, signaled his intention to jump into the race, obviously out of concern at her rise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/merlin_163540113_c3b352b0-4ede-4b35-809b-8628d1bc1bed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/merlin_163540113_c3b352b0-4ede-4b35-809b-8628d1bc1bed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/merlin_163540113_c3b352b0-4ede-4b35-809b-8628d1bc1bed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/merlin_163540113_c3b352b0-4ede-4b35-809b-8628d1bc1bed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1307, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/11tomaskyNew-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/11tomaskyNew-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/11tomaskyNew/11tomaskyNew-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Gates, I Implore You to Connect Some Dots', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'