s Traveler visits the Setouchi Islands, where a triennial art extravaganza is revitalizing fading communities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/travel/52-places-to-go-setouchi-islands-japan.html', 'snippet': 'The 52 Places Traveler visits the Setouchi Islands, where a triennial art extravaganza is revitalizing fading communities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was gray and rainy when two new friends and I walked into a coffee shop on the Japanese island of Shodoshima. Plastic chandeliers hung from a pale-peach ceiling and plush seats were dyed in clashing colors. Beakers and flasks holding bubbling coffee lined the counter. An elderly couple sat at the bar talking to the apron-clad woman who ran the place. An even older man in a wool sweater and reading glasses stared at us, bemused. Behind a plastic screen, another man read the newspaper while puffing on a cigarette. I wondered if they were all here to escape the excitement happening just beyond the doorway.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/travel/12ptg-setouchi-10/12ptg-setouchi-10-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On an Art Scavenger Hunt in Japan’s Seto Inland Sea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On an Art Scavenger Hunt in Japan’s Seto Inland Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDO, TADAO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Ufan (1936- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Naoshima (Kagawa, Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T10:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebastian Modak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebastian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Modak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8d0d40d-0dad-5119-93a6-1cc2dbf49e6d', 'word_count': 2041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8d0d40d-0dad-5119-93a6-1cc2dbf49e6d'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Busted in New York: And Other Essays,” by Darryl Pinckney', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/books/review/busted-in-new-york-and-other-essays-by-darryl-pinckney-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Busted in New York: And Other Essays,” by Darryl Pinckney', 'lead_paragraph': 'When James Baldwin died in 1987, at the age of sixty-three, he was seen as a spent force, a witness for the civil rights movement who had outlived his moment. Baldwin didn’t know when to shut up about the sins of the West, and he went on about them in prose that seemed to lack the grace of voice that had made him famous. But that was the view of him mostly on the white side of town. Ever-militant Amiri Baraka, once scornful of Baldwin as a darling of white liberals, praised “Jimmy” in his eulogy as the creator of a contemporary American speech that we needed in order to talk to one another. Black people have always forgiven and taken back into the tribe the black stars who got kicked out of the Man’s heaven.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Busted in New York: And Other Essays,’ by Darryl Pinckney: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T10:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e64c07ec-1e67-5286-9f59-101a20b3c12b', 'word_count': 3288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e64c07ec-1e67-5286-9f59-101a20b3c12b'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Essays One,” by Lydia Davis', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/books/review/essays-one-by-lydia-davis-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Essays One,” by Lydia Davis', 'lead_paragraph': 'The traditional literary forms—the novel, the short story, the poem—although they evolve, do not disappear. But there is a wealth of less traditional forms that writers have adopted over the decades and centuries, forms that are harder to define and less often encountered, either variations on the more familiar, such as the short-short story, or intergeneric—sitting on a line between poetry and prose, or fable and realistic narrative, or essay and fiction, and so on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Essays One,’ by Lydia Davis: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T10:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d62d025-dd46-59cd-b162-c03e9a0cbdfe', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d62d025-dd46-59cd-b162-c03e9a0cbdfe'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Parisian Lives: Samuel Beckett, Simone de Beauvoir and Me: A Memoir,” by Deirdre Bair', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/books/review/parisian-lives-samuel-beckett-simone-de-beauvoir-and-me-a-memoir-by-deirdre-bair-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Parisian Lives: Samuel Beckett, Simone de Beauvoir and Me: A Memoir,” by Deirdre Bair', 'lead_paragraph': 'As 1981 began, I had ten free days between the holidays and the start of the new semester, when I would begin yet another grueling term of overenrolled courses. I needed those ten days to prepare for the onslaught to come, but it was the only time I could go to Paris. Instead of preparing syllabi, I spent the last days of the old year making increasingly frantic phone calls to hotels along the rue Jacob where I had stayed previously. None would give me a room confirmation, but all told me to come anyway, as something would surely be available. It was an inauspicious start, but I decided to do just that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Parisian Lives: Samuel Beckett, Simone de Beauvoir and Me: A Memoir,’ by Deirdre Bair: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T10:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e097684e-e158-527d-9a83-dfcec95d9bb8', 'word_count': 3355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e097684e-e158-527d-9a83-dfcec95d9bb8'}, {'abstract': "Tuesday: City workers are prepared for the white stuff, although it's not expected to stick, as a cold front brings temperatures plunging toward the 20s.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/nyregion/new-york-city-snow-winter.html', 'snippet': "Tuesday: City workers are prepared for the white stuff, although it's not expected to stick, as a cold front brings temperatures plunging toward the 20s.", 'lead_paragraph': ' [Want to get New York Today by email? Here’s the sign-up.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/nyregion/12nytodayNEW/12nytodayNEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/nyregion/12nytodayNEW/12nytodayNEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/nyregion/12nytodayNEW/12nytodayNEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/nyregion/12nytodayNEW/12nytodayNEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1319, 'width': 2