ent president, Jair Bolsonaro, the liberation of the most beloved and hated man in Brazil threatens to further deepen political tension. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/merlin_164229234_d9c5c132-6bb4-4522-b8a3-484d70a3072d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/merlin_164229234_d9c5c132-6bb4-4522-b8a3-484d70a3072d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/merlin_164229234_d9c5c132-6bb4-4522-b8a3-484d70a3072d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/merlin_164229234_d9c5c132-6bb4-4522-b8a3-484d70a3072d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/12Pires-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/12Pires-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12Pires/12Pires-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lula’s Free. Now What?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Cult of Personality Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Workers' Party (Brazil)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolsonaro, Jair (1955- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Da Silva, Luiz Inacio Lula', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'International Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Pires', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pires', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/522053ac-c0b3-566a-bb97-b164f71834a0', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/522053ac-c0b3-566a-bb97-b164f71834a0'}, {'abstract': 'And did someone say something about impeachment?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/opinion/bloomberg-trump-impeachment.html', 'snippet': 'And did someone say something about impeachment?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: Congratulations, Bret. Michael Bloomberg just stuck his toe in the presidential race. I’m sure he was inspired by our last conversation in which you pleaded for a Bloomberg candidacy. I loved your argument that he had “nothing to lose except 2 percent” of his  net worth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12conversation1/merlin_143851503_8dfbbd4f-cd69-410c-aa2b-8eda0b81e7da-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12conversation1/merlin_143851503_8dfbbd4f-cd69-410c-aa2b-8