nail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12smale/12smale-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12smale/12smale-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Have Advanced to the Same Kind of Mess as Everybody Else’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Communism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eastern Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Havel, Vaclav', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democracy (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Slovakia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caputova, Zuzana', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/55494661-6b71-57fb-bed2-5c3035c4b569', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55494661-6b71-57fb-bed2-5c3035c4b569'}, {'abstract': 'At the New York parade, the question was “Are you booing, or cheering?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/opinion/trump-veterans-day.html', 'snippet': 'At the New York parade, the question was “Are you booing, or cheering?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — A half-moon of garbage trucks rung the southern fringe of Madison Square Park, barriers to keep the parade dignitaries and V.I.P.s insulated from the throng. Loud men with bullhorns moved through the crowd, issuing orders for various veterans groups, while teenage cadets fidgeted in olive drab uniforms that fit their bodies like papier-mâché. The morning smacked of crisp autumn air and rich star-spangled pomp, and for a few seconds at least, I allowed myself to pretend this would be a normal Veterans Day in the city. A day of remembrance, a day of somber celebration, a day of unity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/merlin_164230545_94f0179d-4f75-4248-8c00-7dde38e55d79-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/merlin_164230545_94f0179d-4f75-4248-8c00-7dde38e55d79-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/merlin_164230545_94f0179d-4f75-4248-8c00-7dde38e55d79-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/merlin_164230545_94f0179d-4f75-4248-8c00-7dde38e55d79-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/12gallagher1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/12gallagher1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12gallagher1/12gallagher1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Very Trumpish Veterans Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans Day (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T11:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Gallagher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gallagher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc7edc0d-248c-567b-9bc6-6c7c944e83ee', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc7edc0d-248c-567b-9bc6-6c7c944e83ee'}, {'abstract': 'Quite a few people, and they have something in common. It’s not poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/opinion/elizabeth-warren-billionaires.html', 'snippet': 'Quite a few people, and they have something in common. It’s not poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump has been good for America’s billionaires. He slashed corporate taxes, cut the top income tax rate and raised the total exemption for the estate tax, directly benefiting several hundred billionaires and their heirs. He’s placed wealthy supporters in key positions of government like the Commerce Department, rolled back Obama-era financial regulations and privileged the interests of favored industries — like resource extraction and fossil fuel production — above all else.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/merlin_164237958_d653e911-5caf-479d-85bd-99dc5d0bd6b9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/merlin_164237958_d653e911-5caf-479d-85bd-99dc5d0bd6b9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/merlin_164237958_d653e911-5caf-479d-85bd-99dc5d0bd6b9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/merlin_164237958_d653e911-5caf-479d-85bd-99dc5d0bd6b9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/12bouieWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/12bouieWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/12/opinion/12bouieWeb/12bouieWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who’s Afraid of Elizabeth Warren?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-12T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamelle Bouie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bouie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed4051ce-ea43-5aba-80e6-2c5dd528a04d', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed4051ce-ea43-5aba-80e6-2c5dd528a04d'}, {'abstract': 'The American public values things like fair pay, ethical leadership and job creation. Which companies come out top when judged against those metrics?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/12/business/dealbook/american-companies-values.html', 'snippet': 'The American public values things like fair pay, ethical leadership and job creation. Which companies come out top when judged against those metrics?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good Tuesday. Published in today’s newspaper is a special section dedicated to last week’s DealBook conference. Subscribers to this email got the lowdown last Thursday, but check out the write-ups of ou