ewspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fortress Investment Group L.L.C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Media Investment Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-14T18:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5066cc55-3027-5ec1-b4b7-928e8d827cda', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5066cc55-3027-5ec1-b4b7-928e8d827cda'}, {'abstract': 'Often overlooked in favor of its flashier neighbors, Mykonos and Santorini, the small volcanic isle offers a more peaceful way to experience the Aegean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/t-magazine/milos-greece-travel-guide.html', 'snippet': 'Often overlooked in favor of its flashier neighbors, Mykonos and Santorini, the small volcanic isle offers a more peaceful way to experience the Aegean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milos, the southernmost of the sun-baked Cyclades islands off mainland Greece, is a volcanic oasis home to picturesque whitewashed villages and hidden cliff-ringed coves. Formed around a central caldera and characterized by lunar-like rock formations, it has the highest concentration of beaches in the entire island group — and yet, it’s delightfully untrodden compared to its more famous neighbors, Santorini and Mykonos. It was once a critical location for the mineral trade — during the Neolithic period, the ancient Minoans exported Milos’s obsidian to the neighboring Aegean island of Crete, whose residents used the volcanic glass to make weapons — but the island is best known because of an event from more recent history. It was while digging near the Roman amphitheater in Klima, in 1820, that the amateur archaeologist Olivier Voutier discovered the marble statue known as the “Venus de Milo.” The celebrated work now lives at the Louvre in Paris, but Milos’s mystique remains intact. Thanks to its serene fishing villages, secluded caves, innumerable swimming beaches (many accessible only by boat) and an abundance of locally run restaurants offering fresh catch and regional Greek wines, this tranquil island is quickly gaining appeal for travelers who want Aegean charm without the crowds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM/13tmag-milosguide-slide-BHJM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to Milos, a Greek Island With Fewer Crowds and More Beaches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyclades Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coastal Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AEGEAN SEA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-14T18:19:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michaela Trimble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michaela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trimble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b373d7aa-b967-5847-8593-a868e104bb5c', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b373d7aa-b967-5847-8593-a868e104bb5c'}, {'abstract': 'The writer-director Trey Edward Shults tells the story of a family held together by love and nearly undone by tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/movies/waves-review.html', 'snippet': 'The writer-director Trey Edward Shults tells the story of a family held together by love and nearly undone by tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The camera doesn’t just move in “Waves,” it hurtles with terrific urgency. As you’re swept up in the immersive motion, the kinetic energy, you notice the passing beauty of the images, their compositional elegance. Mostly, though, you just try to keep up as voices boom and the camera pushes in, pulls out, flows in circles or sprints forward. This great whoosh creates a contact high even if, as one shot rapidly gives way to another, it feels as if time is running out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/merlin_164174052_c9d847ee-0a0a-42c7-acc8-3fdd7a45de38-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 249, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/merlin_164174052_c9d847ee-0a0a-42c7-acc8-3fdd7a45de38-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 249}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/merlin_164174052_c9d847ee-0a0a-42c7-acc8-3fdd7a45de38-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/merlin_164174052_c9d847ee-0a0a-42c7-acc8-3fdd7a45de38-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/14waves1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/14waves1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/arts/14waves1/14waves1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Waves’ Review: The Shattering Ebb and Flow of Family Life', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Family Shatters After a Tragic Mistake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Waves (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shults, Trey Edward', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Sterling K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, Kelvin Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-14T18:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2127092e-38cf-508d-be49-24b2ccfa0566', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2127092e-38cf-508d-be49-24b2ccfa0566'}, {'abstract': 'Disney’s latest live-action remake is sweet and tastefully rendered, but it lacks the liveliness of the animated original.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/movies/lady-and-the-tramp-review.html', 'snippet': 'Disney’s latest live-action remake is sweet and tastefully rendered, but it lacks the liveliness of the animated original.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lady and the Tramp” is the fourth live-action remake of an animated Disney hit to come out this year. Unlike “Dumbo,” “Aladdin” and “The Lion King,” however, this latest offering is going straight to streaming as part of the inaugural slate on the new Disney Plus service.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/merlin_163314273_47709b75-ecaf-416a-ac85-7fc490dd6257-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/merlin_163314273_47709b75-ecaf-416a-ac85-7fc490dd6257-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/merlin_163314273_47709b75-ecaf-416a-ac85-7fc490dd6257-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/merlin_163314273_47709b75-ecaf-416a-ac85-7fc490dd6257-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 1210, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/14ladyandthetramp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/14ladyandthetramp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/arts/14ladyandthetramp/14ladyandthetramp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lady and the Tramp’ Review: Seconds of Spaghetti and Furballs', 'kicker': 'Streaming Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pooch Romance, And Still al Dente', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disney Plus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lady and the Tramp (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-14T18:31:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Vincentelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vincentelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b76f20cc-f289-5c69-9b26-fc0d9f8d2d50', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b76f20cc-f289-5c69-9b26-fc0d9f8d2d50'}, {'abstract': 'At 15, my grandmother was locked up alongside young women committed for “immorality.” Her story taught me about a little-known history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/opinion/teen-girls-jailed.html', 'snippet': 'At 15, my grandmother was locked up alongside young women committed for “immorality.” Her story taught me about a little-known history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1932, at the age of 12, my maternal grandmother, a talented young singer, was a victim of sexual abuse. By the time she was 15, she was performing in a Minneapolis nightclub to earn money to help her family survive. It was the Depression, and she was the youngest daughter of a widowed mother, a Norwegian immigrant seamstress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 533}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1820, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/14/opinion/sunday/14oconnor-sub/14oconnor-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When ‘Incorrigible’ Teen Girls Were Jailed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Criminal Justice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-14T18:35:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By Sheila O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb6cca70-6051-5639-85d4-e9afb929cac1', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb6cca70-6051-5639-85d4-e9afb929cac1'}, {'abstract': 'Our advice columnist explains to a reader the trouble with armchair diagnoses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/style/autism-diagnosis.html', 'snippet': 'Our advice columnist explains to a reader the trouble with armchair diagnoses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My sister is in her 50s. She suffers (and has benefited) from autism spectrum disorder. It’s given her brilliance at the expense of social functioning. Sadly, she is not aware of her A.S.D. or formally diagnosed. But she gets furious if anyone challenges her; she is unable to forgive small slights and doesn’t perceive other people’s intentions correctly. I think she would benefit from understanding her condition, but she brushed off my suggestion that she is on the spectrum. Meanwhile, she is alienating herself from our family with her behavior. I feel like shouting: “You have Asperger’s! Embrace it!” How can we fix this situation?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inli