inal': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea15a650-0d67-5956-8f06-a5af24154866', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea15a650-0d67-5956-8f06-a5af24154866'}, {'abstract': 'Amy Yoder Begley says she was criticized for being overweight, told her laugh was annoying and made to sign a contract promising not to become friends with her teammates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/sports/olympics/alberto-salazar-nike.html', 'snippet': 'Amy Yoder Begley says she was criticized for being overweight, told her laugh was annoying and made to sign a contract promising not to become friends with her teammates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Amy Yoder Begley, an Olympic middle-distance runner, four tumultuous years with Alberto Salazar’s Nike Oregon Project came to an abrupt end in September 2011. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/sports/14begley1/merlin_164343996_c1dec5bb-0fd7-4d39-8eb8-7e6de1861c40-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/14/sports/14begley1/merlin_164343996_c1dec5bb-0fd7-4d39-8eb8-7e6de1861c40-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 739}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/sports/14begley1/merlin_164343996_c1dec5bb-0fd7-4d39-8eb8-7e6de1861c40-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/14/sports/14begley1/merlin_164343996_c1dec5