, Okla. — On a recent Friday afternoon, in the parking lot of a Dollar General in the North Tulsa neighborhood of Greenwood, Jessica Faulk loaded a frozen pizza and other snacks for her grandkids into her car. This was her first trip to the store, which sits near an elementary school and a housing complex for seniors. Though she lives nearby, she’d been avoiding the retailer for more than a year out of principle, and usually shops at a Walmart in the suburb of Sand Springs. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/opinion/17luck2/merlin_164012442_4037a865-7feb-4ae7-99c2-8db6bb0aae6c-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How a City Fought Runaway Capitalism and Won', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Tulsa Fought Capitalism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dollar General Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tulsa (Okla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-15T16:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Luckerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luckerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/465974d2-6923-5873-969b-37e4a61126fd', 'word_count': 1644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/465974d2-6923-5873-969b-37e4a61126fd'}, {'abstract': 'For more than a thousand years, the country’s cherry blossom season has been a source of fascination and wonderment. How did such an infatuation begin?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/15/t-magazine/japan-cherry-blossoms.html', 'snippet': 'For more than a thousand years, the country’s cherry blossom season has been a source of fascination and wonderment. How did such an infatuation begin?', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE SCENE IS a park in the late afternoon. It is springtime: The trees are a profound, almost bluish emerald; the first reeds are beginning to sprout in the river. The sky is a soft, worn, denimy blue, although above a smudge of cloud is a stripe of near black — it will rain soon. Yet there is no sense of doom, no portent; the rain, you sense, will be welcome when it arrives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1922, 'width': 1926, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT/15tmag-japan-slide-HSYT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan in Bloom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spring (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hiroshige', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanagihara, Hanya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kyoto (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cherries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-15T16:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanya Yanagihara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yanagihara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d405f9b3-baba-509f-9e4f-2a4ed9eaca68', 'word_count': 3638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d405f9b3-baba-509f-9e4f-2a4ed9eaca68'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Warren laid out a blueprint to pass major health legislation at the start of her presidency. But she would wait as long as three years to seek passage of a full-scale “Medicare for all” plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/15/us/politics/elizabeth-warren-medicare-for-all-100-days.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Warren laid out a blueprint to pass major health legislation at the start of her presidency. But she would wait as long as three years to seek passage of a full-scale “Medicare for all” plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senator Elizabeth Warren vowed on Friday to pass major health care legislation in her first 100 days as president, unveiling a new, detailed plan to significantly expand public health insurance coverage as a first step, and promising to pass a “Medicare for all” system by the end of her third year in office that would cover all Americans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/merlin_164233896_e66af0c5-6c52-42ac-90d3-5ae637f827e6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/merlin_164233896_e66af0c5-6c52-42ac-90d3-5ae637f827e6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/merlin_164233896_e66af0c5-6c52-42ac-90d3-5ae637f827e6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/merlin_164233896_e66af0c5-6c52-42ac-90d3-5ae637f827e6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/15warren-medicare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/15warren-medicare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/15/us/politics/15warren-medicare/1