alue': 'Trump-Ukraine Whistle-blower Complaint and Impeachment Inquiry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impeachment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yovanovitch, Marie L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-15T19:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e623a9b-bbb9-5f00-82fb-38394acf8e4a', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e623a9b-bbb9-5f00-82fb-38394acf8e4a'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of things our editors — and a few contributors — are excited about in a given week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/15/t-magazine/mike-kelley-timeless-painting-tiina-cashmere-editors-picks.html', 'snippet': 'A roundup of things our editors — and a few contributors — are excited about in a given week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hauser & Wirth has spent the last few years breaking down the complex career of Mike Kelley, the Detroit-born, Los Angeles-based artist who died by suicide in 2012. If there is a steady theme throughout Kelley’s diverse work, it is his chameleonic ability to leap between genres and methods. He used video, drawing, installation, sculpture and found objects — sometimes all in the course of a single piece — to examine the darkest corners of his own subconscious and memory, often hinting at a mysterious, unspoken trauma that is revisited again and again but never quite defined. Kelley was a conceptual trickster so subtle and clever that in the gallery’s latest view of him, an exhibition called “Timeless Painting,” curated by Jenelle Porter, the word painting itself is delivered with a knowing wink.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/t-magazine/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P/15tmag-tel-slide-0U4P-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'