ger root. The harsh taste comforts her. Texas is an unknown, vast and strange, but as readers of Thanhha Lai’s searingly beautiful BUTTERFLY YELLOW (Harper/HarperCollins, 284 pp., $17.99; ages 12 and up) will soon learn, Hang is a refugee. She is familiar with bitter things.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 906}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1687, 'width': 1117, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/books/review/17-BKS-Donnelley/17-BKS-Donnelley-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline