ect', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buckingham Palace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andrew, Duke of York', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epstein, Jeffrey E (1953- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuffre, Virginia Roberts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-16T00:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Specia and Neil Vigdor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Specia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vigdor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c35c4e-51d0-500c-9ff8-0c37bacf3be5', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c35c4e-51d0-500c-9ff8-0c37bacf3be5'}, {'abstract': 'Thiem has won five titles this year and reached the semifinals of the ATP Finals, where only one member of the so-called Big Three stands in his way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/15/sports/tennis/dominic-thiem-atp-finals.html', 'snippet': 'Thiem has won five titles this year and reached the semifinals of the ATP Finals, where only one member of the so-called Big Three stands in his way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Dominic Thiem will not admit to being superstitious. He said his 5-year-old habit of twirling the tennis ball around in his fingers before every serve is no different than Alexander Zverev tugging at his shirt in between points or Rafael Nadal lining up his bottles in perfect order beside his chair. It is simply part of his routine.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/merlin_164380524_5dc18304-457d-4009-9feb-1c937de455c0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/merlin_164380524_5dc18304-457d-4009-9feb-1c937de455c0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/merlin_164380524_5dc18304-457d-4009-9feb-1c937de455c0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/merlin_164380524_5dc18304-457d-4009-9feb-1c937de455c0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/16-TENNIS-PRINT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/16-TENNIS-PRINT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/16/sports/16-TENNIS-PRINT/16-TENNIS-PRINT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy