i': 'nyt://article/5c35424b-59fb-5de1-971f-d1f61208cb42'}, {'abstract': 'John Bel Edwards of Louisiana, a rare Democratic governor in the South, was re-elected for a second term, beating back a challenger heavily supported by President Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/16/us/louisiana-governor-edwards-rispone.html', 'snippet': 'John Bel Edwards of Louisiana, a rare Democratic governor in the South, was re-elected for a second term, beating back a challenger heavily supported by President Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BATON ROUGE, La. — Gov. John Bel Edwards of Louisiana, the only Democratic governor in the Deep South, narrowly won re-election Saturday, overcoming the intervention of President Trump, who visited the state multiple times in an effort to help Mr. Edwards’s Republican challenger and demonstrate his own clout.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Louisiana, a Narrow Win for John Bel Edwards and a Hard Loss for Trump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Louisiana, Governor’s Victory Shows Limits of Trump’s Support', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, John Bel (1966- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rispone, Eddie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-16T22:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas and Jeremy Alford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reporte