ed', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c02344b4-f8c2-52c4-936c-8333deaeb5ae', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c02344b4-f8c2-52c4-936c-8333deaeb5ae'}, {'abstract': 'Practice for Thanksgiving, and make Alexa Weibel’s vegetarian mushroom Wellington. Or keep it weeknight, with hot-sauce roast chicken and salmon burgers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/17/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Practice for Thanksgiving, and make Alexa Weibel’s vegetarian mushroom Wellington. Or keep it weeknight, with hot-sauce roast chicken and salmon burgers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. There are some among us wondering, and not for the first time, what we’re going to serve on Thanksgiving to please those who don’t eat meat. We have no shortage of vegetarian recipes for side dishes, and for casseroles that punch above their weight in terms of protein and beauty. But a glamorous vegetarian centerpiece for the Thanksgiving table, the plant-based equivalent of a bronzed turkey, a dish born for fame and fortune, an actual star? We are always and forever looking for that. It’s a rare gem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/23/dining/aw-mushroom-wellington-copy/merlin_163633167_473a653a-a909-42e2-94c3-0788f950a163-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/23/dining/aw-mushroom-wellington-copy/merlin_163633167_473a653a-a909-42e2-94c3-0788f950a163-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/23/dining/aw-mushroom-wellington-copy/merlin_163633167_473a653a-a909-42e2-94c3-0788f950a163-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':