:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4329af63-f2a6-55b2-9622-5c9ac24d3e5e', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4329af63-f2a6-55b2-9622-5c9ac24d3e5e'}, {'abstract': 'As nationalized as our media environment has become, it’s still true in some cases that “all politics is local,” as the old phrase goes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/18/opinion/louisiana-governor-trump.html', 'snippet': 'As nationalized as our media environment has become, it’s still true in some cases that “all politics is local,” as the old phrase goes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — On Saturday, John Bel Edwards, the governor of Louisiana, beat the Trump-aligned Republican businessman Eddie Rispone in a tight race, winning a second term, thanks in large part to a boost from tightly concentrated but highly populated deep-blue precincts in the southeast. Especially here in New Orleans, where nearly 50 percent of voters turned out — the highest level in years — and handed 90 percent of their votes to the incumbent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/17/us/politics/17louisiana-trump-02/merlin_162612540_6314ea7f-57ce-49ed-8c47-d8fe08d8857f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Bel Edwards Wasn’t a Soul Mate, but a Perfect Match in Louisiana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, John Bel (1966- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-18T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katy Reckdahl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reckdahl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d0e0dd-08ce-5c52-ab2f-9b70afebb4dd', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d0e0dd-08ce-5c52-ab2f-9b70afebb4dd'}, {'abstract': 'We can’t dismiss good ideas because they don’t fit into neat ideological boxes or don’t personally affect some of the louder, more privileged voices in the party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/18/opinion/cory-booker-public-charter-schools.html', 'snippet': 'We can’t dismiss good ideas because they don’t fit into neat ideological boxes or don’t personally affect some of the louder, more privileged voices in the party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 15 years ago, when I was living in Brick Towers, a high-rise, low-income housing community in Newark’s Central Ward, a neighbor stopped me and told me about how her child’s public school was failing its students, like many others in our area at the time. Desperate, she asked if I knew a way to help get her child into a private school. She knew, as all parents do, that a great education was her child’s primary pathway to a better life.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/merlin_164473893_6a434cc2-edb0-4bf6-adcf-80fea7d71466-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/merlin_164473893_6a434cc2-edb0-4bf6-adcf-80fea7d71466-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/merlin_164473893_6a434cc2-edb0-4bf6-adcf-80fea7d71466-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/merlin_164473893_6a434cc2-edb0-4bf6-adcf-80fea7d71466-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/18bookerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/18bookerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18bookerWeb/18bookerWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cory Booker: Stop Being Dogmatic About Public Charter Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charter Schools Deserve a Fair Hearing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-18T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cory A. Booker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cory', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Booker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ead47684-c578-5398-ad13-e2b9402546b7', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ead47684-c578-5398-ad13-e2b9402546b7'}, {'abstract': 'The secretary of state’s behavior has been cowardly and self-serving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/18/opinion/mike-pompeo.html', 'snippet': 'The secretary of state’s behavior has been cowardly and self-serving.', 'lead_paragraph': ' It seems like every story you read about Secretary of State Mike Pompeo always includes the sentence that he graduated “first in his class” from West Point. That is not a small achievement. But it is even more impressive in Pompeo’s case when you consider that he finished No. 1 even though he must have flunked all his courses on ethics and leadership. I guess he was really good in math.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18friedman1/18friedman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18friedman1/18friedman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18friedman1/18friedman1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18friedman1/18friedman1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18friedman1/18friedman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/18/opinion/18friedman1/18friedman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/1