ndard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/arts/18bronte-item/18bronte-item-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tiny Brontë Book Comes Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiny Brontë Book Returning to England', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronte, Charlotte', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BRONTE SOCIETY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronte Parsonage Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-18T22:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93f36b4d-f19f-5226-9682-ab631fdae4c7', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93f36b4d-f19f-5226-9682-ab631fdae4c7'}, {'abstract': 'The Cookmobile, a kitchen on wheels, teaches Brooklyn Public Library patrons how to cook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/18/dining/cookmobile-brooklyn-library.html', 'snippet': 'The Cookmobile, a kitchen on wheels, teaches Brooklyn Public Library patrons how to cook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn Public Library runs a wealth of programs, among them the Cookmobile, which offers free cooking classes for high schoolers, particularly in neighborhoods where fresh ingredients are in short supply. A compact 5-by-3-by-2-foot unit funded by the Bklyn Incubator, the Cookmobile is fitted with a sink, induction cooktop, convection oven and enough cooking utensils for up to 30 students. It can be transported from place to place and wheeled right into the library, ready for a class. “We even have a Vitamix,” said Johanna Lewis, a librarian who teaches the classes with Adeeba Rana, also a librarian. Last week, there were eight students, mostly boys, some of whom were repeats. They learned to make coleslaw and jollof rice, with some cultural background and even a brief food science lesson from Ms. Rana. Cookmobile has been holding classes at the Cypress Hills branch on Thursdays from 3:30 to 5 p.m. After Thanksgiving, it will move to another branch, yet to be determined, for six weeks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/dining/18burner6/merlin_164458464_543da2ee-23c3-403b-979f-3771c7362b65-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/20/dining/18burner6/merlin_164458464_543da2ee-23c3-403b-979f-3771c7362b65-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/dining/18burner6/merlin_164458464_543da2ee-23c3-403b-979f-3771c7362b65-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/dining/18burner6/merlin_164458464_543da2ee-23c3-403b-979f-3771c7362b65-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,