0', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b598770c-4433-5ed4-9984-172b88508be6', 'word_count': 2331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b598770c-4433-5ed4-9984-172b88508be6'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “The Second Sleep,” by Robert Harris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/19/books/review/the-second-sleep-by-robert-harris-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “The Second Sleep,” by Robert Harris', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late on the afternoon of Tuesday the ninth of April in the Year of Our Risen Lord 1468, a solitary traveller was to be observed picking his way on horseback across the wild moorland of that ancient region of southwestern England known since Saxon times as Wessex. If this young man’s expression was troubled, we may grant he had good cause. More than an hour had elapsed since he had last seen a living soul. Soon it would be dusk, and if he was caught out of doors after curfew he risked a night in jail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Second Sleep,’ by Robert Harris: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-19T10:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f32c3e-adca-5470-921d-7e946a912e14', 'word_count': 1685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f32c3e-adca-5470-921d-7e946a912e14'}, {'abstract': 'The South Carolina city is known for its historic homes and traditional Southern charm, but it’s also a place where new design is flourishing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/19/realestate/the-charleston-you-h