itchen and bathroom, looking for nitroglycerin, the only medicine that relieved the pain. She couldn’t read the labels on the pill bottles — that’s when she knew she was in real trouble. She could feel her heart beating erratically as she called 911. She collapsed before she could even unlock the door.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1676, 'width': 1676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-diagnosis-1/24mag-diagnosis-1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'She Had Two Heart Attacks, but Normal Arteries. What Was Going On?', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Canker Sores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ulcers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-20T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f299fbf-8264-5305-a48e-1709ed8e2549', 'word_count': 1339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f299fbf-8264-5305-a48e-1709ed8e2549'}, {'abstract': 'On Instagram, “mom” means linen-clad babies and perfect homes. On TikTok, it’s real women being their wholesome, goofy selves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/20/magazine/tiktok-mom.html', 'snippet': 'On Instagram, “mom” means linen-clad babies and perfect homes. On TikTok, it’s real women being their wholesome, goofy selves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rural or rural-seeming scene: In the foreground, in the lower left-hand corner of the frame, a cherubic middle-aged woman with short blond hair and a friendly, expressive face holds up an index finger. Behind her, a man with a paunch and a handlebar mustache emerges from a black truck just as she starts to lip-sync the 1997 song “My Baby Daddy,” by B-Rock and the Bizz. You’d guess he’s her husband, and he’s obviously a good sport. As he saunters toward the front of the truck, the woman tickles the air in his general direction. He leans on a headlight and smiles. They are corny, playful, in that goofy parental way that makes kids groan in embarrassment.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-jumbo.png', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-screenland-1/24mag-screenland-1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Moms of TikTok Are Deeply Corny — and Gloriously Free', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apro