e, “Duet for Cannibals,” a dry comedy made in Sweden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/21/movies/duet-for-cannibals-susan-sontag.html', 'snippet': 'The author and public intellectual wrestled with a new medium and a foreign language in her now restored first feature, “Duet for Cannibals,” a dry comedy made in Sweden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1969 New York Film Festival was the first to feature four movies directed by women and three made in Swedish. Susan Sontag’s “Duet for Cannibals,” which she wrote and directed, fit both categories. Given the chance to make her debut film in the land of the reigning cinematic genius Ingmar Bergman, Sontag seized the opportunity to direct in a foreign language while supplying her own English subtitles. In those days her name was synonymous with zeitgeist.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/22/arts/21rewind/merlin_164629809_c41e3e9f-ed0f-47c6-98c7-1b08c2df5925-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/22/arts/21rewind/merlin_164629809_c41e3e9f-ed0f-47c6-98c7-1b08c2df5925-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/22/arts/21rewind/merlin_164629809_c41e3e9f-ed0f-47c6-98c7-1b08c2df5925-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/22/arts/21rewind/merlin_164629809_c41e3e9f-ed0f-47c6-98c7-1b08c2df5925-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1245, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i