hird collection of poems, “This American Autopsy,” José Antonio Rodríguez examines what it means to be on the edge, between nationalities, acceptances and dismissals by la migra — immigration agents. When did anxiety become a birthright for whole groups of people? From the very beginning? How has a country made of immigrants come to this current moment of walls and detention facilities? His poems are humanizing testaments of life, penetrating headlines, inviting readers into real rooms and families. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-poem-1/24mag-poem-1-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-poem-1/24mag-poem-1-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-poem-1/24mag-poem-1-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 494, 'width': 958, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-poem-1/24mag-poem-1-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 494, 'width': 958, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-poem-1/24mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/24/magazine/24mag-poem-1/24mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima