essure campaign to Russian efforts to sow political divisions in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/21/us/politics/fiona-hill-impeachment-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'The former top White House aide denounced a theory that Ukraine interfered in the 2016 election, as she tied the president’s pressure campaign to Russian efforts to sow political divisions in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A former White House Russia expert on Thursday sharply denounced a “fictional narrative” embraced by President Trump and his Republican allies that Ukraine, not Russia, interfered in the 2016 election, testifying that the claim was a fabrication by Moscow that had harmed the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiona Hill Testifies ‘Fictions’ on Ukraine Pushed by Trump Help Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expert Condemns Flow of “Fictions’ on Ukraine’s Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trump-Ukraine Whistle-blower Complaint and Impeachment Inquiry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Fiona (1965- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-21T20:34:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Fandos and Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nichola