are a unified impulse, a perfect whole, and every time she improvises, the history of tap meets its cutting edge.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/merlin_164299284_df8bdb40-3d58-4aa5-bbbe-c0e2526fd978-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/merlin_164299284_df8bdb40-3d58-4aa5-bbbe-c0e2526fd978-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/merlin_164299284_df8bdb40-3d58-4aa5-bbbe-c0e2526fd978-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/merlin_164299284_df8bdb40-3d58-4aa5-bbbe-c0e2526fd978-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/24dormeshia5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/24dormeshia5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/24/arts/24dormeshia5/24dormeshia5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s the Queen of Tap. Is Her Moment Now?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who’s That Tapping at Culture’s Window?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sumbry-Edwards, Dormeshia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'And Still You Must Swing (Dance)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz Tap Ensemble', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Jason Samuels', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Derick K (1973- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-22T15:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d7ebfc-38f6-597d-9076-2a7555b8ca5e', 'word_count': 1567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d7ebfc-38f6-597d-9076-2a7555b8ca5e'}, {'abstract': 'It’s time for Broadway to embrace what’s most joyous about songbook shows. Not biography, not coherence, but excess. Even “Moulin Rouge!” doesn’t quite get it right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/22/theater/broadway-pop-musicals.html', 'snippet': 'It’s time for Broadway to embrace what’s most joyous about songbook shows. Not biography, not coherence, but excess. Even “Moulin Rouge!” doesn’t quite get it right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes, I crave a musical where grandiosity is unencumbered by logic and good taste. I don’t need a book that makes sense when I can feast on eye-popping visuals backed by an eardrum-busting sound system. It’s O.K. for the brain to take a rest while the senses work overtime. Broadway knew that once, or at least Florenz Ziegfeld did.',