crowns a winner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/25/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday-slings-arrows-and-the-dancing-with-the-stars-finale.html', 'snippet': 'The second season of the Canadian comedy series is now available. And the dance competition crowns a winner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SLINGS & ARROWS Stream on Acorn TV. In Season 1 of this cult-favorite Canadian comedy from the 2000s, Geoffrey Tennant (Paul Gross) is lured back to the Shakespearean theater festival he had fled when its artistic director, Oliver Welles (Stephen Ouimette), dies unexpectedly. Geoffrey tries to make his peace with Oliver, who appears to him as a ghost, and Ellen Fanshaw (Martha Burns), his former lover, while he works to save a production of “Hamlet.” Season 2, which is available beginning Monday, revolves around “Macbeth,” a play whose difficulty begins to threaten Geoffrey’s sanity. While Geoffrey deals with artistic issues, Richard Smith-Jones (Mark McKinney), the festival’s manager, struggles with a new advertising campaign and Ellen is forced to deal with the tax authorities. The third and final season will be available Dec. 16. Margaret Lyons, a Times TV critic, recently wrote: “It’s one of my favorite shows ever, and one that gets better and better the more you watch it.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/arts/25tvcol-slings/merlin_163914294_205a1bcf-9928-475a-9d21-c26044773a19-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/25/arts/25tvcol-slings/merlin_163914294_205a1bcf-9928-475a-9d21-c26044773a19-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/arts/25tvcol-slings/merlin_163914294_205a1bcf-9928