, whose murder conviction nearly 20 years ago formed the basis of the hit podcast “Serial.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/multimedia/25xp-serial/25xp-serial-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Serial’ Podcast Case Is Declined by Supreme Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Syed, Adnan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Serial (Radio Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Hae Min (1980-99)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-25T16:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Zraick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zraick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b827de-2b94-5fba-abdb-5d0b26029ebe', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b827de-2b94-5fba-abdb-5d0b26029ebe'}, {'abstract': 'We asked holiday hosts around the country to show us how they serve the feast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/25/dining/thanksgiving-table-decor.html', 'snippet': 'We asked holiday hosts around the country to show us how they serve the feast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Color, form and playful provocation are Peter Shire’s visual language — even at the Thanksgiving table. The painter, sculptor, ceramist and furniture designer was one of the founding members of the Memphis design group, and his work is in museums around the world. Every year, he hosts 30 people in his Echo X Park Artist Studio space, adding on to the table that his father, Henry, built in 1950, which has been used for every family Thanksgiving since.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25Tables1/25Tables1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25T