': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zucchino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fatima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Faizi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd9c58f5-e7f7-5585-84fb-2a87c3e93e10', 'word_count': 1576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd9c58f5-e7f7-5585-84fb-2a87c3e93e10'}, {'abstract': 'The acclaimed restaurant now sells its biscuits, ready to reheat, nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/25/dining/frozen-biscuits-the-grey.html', 'snippet': 'The acclaimed restaurant now sells its biscuits, ready to reheat, nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Occupying a repurposed Greyhound bus terminal, the Grey in Savannah, Ga., is a highly regarded restaurant with New York roots. Its owners, John O. Morisano, and Mashama Bailey, the executive chef and partner, are both from the city, though Ms. Bailey’s family originally came from Georgia. Now, the ethereal biscuits for which she is known are being sold nationwide. They come frozen, ready to bake without thawing. The plain ones are generous rounds. The square, flavored ones are fragrant with honey and herbs, tangy with chopped Southern greens or oozing pimento cheese.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1116, 'width': 1482, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner6/25burner6-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Make’ the Biscuits From the Grey in Savannah', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Bake: ‘Make’ the Biscuits  From the Grey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grey, The (Savannah, Ga, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mail Order Companies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldbelly Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-25T16:22:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef5fbc92-8fe1-58d3-a670-c22350969666', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef5fbc92-8fe1-58d3-a670-c22350969666'}, {'abstract': 'A Colorado distillery picks up its empty vodka bottles from bars and restaurants to give them another life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/25/dining/mell-zero-waste-vodka.html', 'snippet': 'A Colorado distillery picks up its empty vodka bottles from bars and restaurants to give them another life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The demand for a no-waste lifestyle has led a distiller, Jack Rabbit Hill Farm in Hotchkiss, Colo., to come up with a clever way to minimize trash. Not content with having the empties of its MEll vodka hauled away from the bars and restaurants, where most of it is sold, the company picks them up as the milkman once did — at the back door. The bottles are sterilized in the distillery and reused to bottle more vodka. Lance Hanson, an owner, knows that a bartender cannot legally refill an empty liquor bottle, but the distillery can. As for the vodka, sold mostly in Colorado, it’s straightforward, no bells and whistles.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 222, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 222}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner5/25burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Like the Milkman, This Distiller Refills the Empties', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Recycle: A Vodka Distiller  Refills the Empties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hotchkiss (Colo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vodka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jack Rabbit Hill Farm', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanson, Lance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-25T16:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3c37195-300c-5220-8595-7c41f2c3e54c', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3c37195-300c-5220-8595-7c41f2c3e54c'}, {'abstract': '“Sushi Modoki,” a new cookbook, offers insights for creating nigiri, rolls, chirashi and molded sushi without meat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/25/dining/sushi-modoki-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '“Sushi Modoki,” a new cookbook, offers insights for creating nigiri, rolls, chirashi and molded sushi without meat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the New York company Beyond Sushi has been selling and serving dazzling vegan sushi, and now there’s a book on the subject. “Sushi Modoki: The Japanese Art and Craft of Vegan Sushi” by Iina, a Japanese chef working in Tokyo. Modoki means “to mimic” in Japanese, the book explains, and that’s precisely what the recipes do, substituting tomato or red bell pepper for tuna, carrot for salmon, mushroom stems for scallops and kabocha squash for sea urchin. Various formats, including nigiri, rolls, chirashi and molded sushi are covered, as are stocks and condiments. The results are worth the time and patience they require; alas, they’ll be consumed in a flash.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 1010, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/dining/25burner1/25burner1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Learn to Make Vegan Sushi', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Prepare: For Vegan Sushi, Just Turn the Page', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sushi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veganism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sushi Modoki: The Japanese Art and Craft of Vegan Sushi (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iina (Chef)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-25T16:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a68d67a-962e-5b9a-a359-e7635a1e3f9f', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a68d67a-962e-5b9a-a359-e7635a1e3f9f'}, {'abstract': 'The consumer-direct company Material now sells sturdy stainless-steel shears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/25/dining/the-good-shears-scissors.html', 'snippet': 'The consumer-direct company Material now sells sturdy stainless-steel shears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joyce Chen kitchen shears have been my do-it-all utensil for decades. 