age', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-26T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Concepción de León', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Concepción', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de León', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4008572a-be98-54c4-8f29-5926b54c2f11', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4008572a-be98-54c4-8f29-5926b54c2f11'}, {'abstract': 'To sensitize toddlers’ fingertips, hide little objects in sand or rice. Label objects around the home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/26/magazine/how-to-teach-a-child-braille.html', 'snippet': 'To sensitize toddlers’ fingertips, hide little objects in sand or rice. Label objects around the home.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Encourage exploration with the hands,” says Jackie Anderson, who taught blind students in Cobb County, Ga., for a decade and helped develop the National Federation of the Blind’s nationwide summer program for blind children. Advocates point to what they call a Braille literacy crisis in America, despite research showing that visually impaired people have better employment and educational outcomes if they read and write Braille. To decode Braille’s little bumps, you need highly sensitized fingertips. Help toddlers hone their tactile awareness by burying little objects like marbles, toy cars and small figurines in a sand dish or bowl of rice. Tell the child to find and match them.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1041, 'width': 1754, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Teach a Child Braille', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Teach A Child Braille', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Braille', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-26T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d110505f-3881-5f14-8b8e-41b556ee18d5', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d110505f-3881-5f14-8b8e-41b556ee18d5'}, {'abstract': 'How a hedge fund’s efforts to take the island territory to the cleaners wound up before the Supreme Court — with ordinary Puerto Ricans arguing in the hedge fund’s favor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/26/magazine/aurelius-capital-v-puerto-rico.html', 'snippet': 'How a hedge fund’s efforts to take the island territory to the cleaners wound up before the Supreme Court — with ordinary Puerto Ricans arguing in the hedge fund’s favor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Puerto Rico filed for bankruptcy protection at 11:32 in the morning on May 3, 2017; by 11:33, the magnitude was obvious. No American territory had ever defaulted on so much debt. “A bankruptcy without precedent” ran a morning-after headline in the tabloid El Vocero, in an issue that also quoted leftist politicians warning readers not to be fooled: The filing, they claimed, was a prelude to more austerity. The island owed $72 billion. Already there was out-migration of 60,000 people a year and 10.5 percent unemployment. There were reports that vendors, owed millions of dollars, would no longer deliver food to Puerto Rican prisons.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '43', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 646}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01mag-aurelius-01/01mag-aurelius-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Curious Case of Aurelius Capital v. Puerto Rico', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Isle of Debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vulture Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Maria (2017)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aurelius Capital Management', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brodsky, Mark D', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-26T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00db93c6-080a-5bc3-aa24-f9d330c763dc', 'word_count': 3643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00db93c6-080a-5bc3-aa24-f9d330c763dc'}, {'abstract': 'We selected four articles from The Times that each takes on a different perspective about the holiday. Which resonates the most with your experience?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/26/learning/what-does-thanksgiving-mean-to-you.html', 'snippet': 'We selected four articles from The Times that each takes on a different perspective about the holiday. Which resonates the most with your experience?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you looking forward to Thanksgiving? Or do you dread the holiday? Do you have certain Thanksgiving traditions? Do you think they are the same or different for other people in your school or community?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14first1/merlin_145873443_5a8b2317-8e16-459b-b1a7-c546e86c598e-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does Thanksgiving Mean to You?', 'kicker': 'student opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-26T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Daniels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daniels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cb6742a-a7e1-5757-a11b-b5e410be4522', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cb6742a-a7e1-5757-a11b-b5e410be4522'}, {'abstract': 'Who would have guessed that magic’s most recognizable buddy pair would produce the classiest reality show on television?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/26/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-penn-teller-fool-us.html', 'snippet': 'Who would have guessed that magic’s most recognizable buddy pair would produce the classiest reality show on television?', 'lead_paragraph': '“Penn & Teller: Fool Us” is a reality-TV competition shown on the CW, which is a broadcast network, which is something like a streaming service that’s always on. The show was recently renewed for its seventh season. The only other person I know who watches it is a skilled amateur magician and general magic geek who lives in Chicago. For him, the show is a chance to be exposed to some of the world’s greatest magicians and get an insight into their arcane techniques. For me, who doesn’t particularly like magic and has no intention of trying to do it, the show has a different appeal: It makes me a better person.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-LOR-1/01Mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-LOR-1/01Mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-LOR-1/01Mag-LOR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-LOR-1/01Mag-LOR-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1516, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-LOR-1/01Mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/01/magazine/01Mag-LOR-1/01Mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'