urs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flames Coach Accused of Using Racial Slurs on Player in the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calgary Flames', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Bill (1966- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aliu, Akim (1989- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-26T20:17:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49c4ac56-90e5-5531-a596-011a20e7fd71', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49c4ac56-90e5-5531-a596-011a20e7fd71'}, {'abstract': 'Mel Bochner, who has spent half a century making art, revisits one of his early shows for his latest exhibition at Dia:Beacon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/26/t-magazine/mel-bochner.html', 'snippet': 'Mel Bochner, who has spent half a century making art, revisits one of his early shows for his latest exhibition at Dia:Beacon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gallery is hangar-size and vacant, seemingly poised to receive a monumental sculpture or house an epic-scale theatrical production; a commuter train would fit quite snugly. But, on an early November morning inside Dia:Beacon, the Hudson Valley, N.Y., museum known for its exhibitions of Minimalist art, none of that awaits. In fact, the work is already installed: Thick lines of red tape course along the sunlit walls, accompanied by numbers that reflect their respective measurements (3’, 16’8”), like a blueprint come to life. “Measurement Room: No Vantage Point” by Mel Bochner, which opened at the museum this month, is the artist’s latest effort in making our thought processes visible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3/26tmag-Bochner-slide-FKL3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75