or sour majesty. What she wanted, she once said, was to communicate “what it’s like to be inside this particular skull.” Forty years after her death, her sentences still gleam like knives.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1397, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/books/26bookstafford2/26bookstafford2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jean Stafford’s Novels Frankly Survey the Kingdom of Childhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childhood World  In All Its Taboos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'STAFFORD, JEAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Boston Adventure (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Catherine Wheel (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Mountain Lion (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-26T20:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Parul Sehgal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Parul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sehgal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d035050-3ad9-52d4-8cf8-6bac00348fa3', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d035050-3ad9-52d4-8cf8-6bac00348fa3'}, {'abstract': 'Five new books take us to far-flung places including Mexico, Tasmania, the Alaskan tundra and Hays, Kan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2019/books/travel-books-gifts.html', 'snippet': 'Five new books take us to far-flung places including Mexico, Tasmania, the Alaskan tundra and Hays, Kan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five new books take us to far-flung places including Mexico, Tasmania, the Alaskan tundra and Hays, Kan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/08/books/HolidayBooksTravel/HolidayBooksTravel-articleLarge-v7.png', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/08/books/HolidayBooksTravel/HolidayBooksTravel-articleLarge-v7.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'r