_paragraph': 'An article on March 6, 2018, about Judge Dan Aaron Polster’s strategy for addressing hundreds of lawsuits tied to the opioid crisis, gave an incomplete description of Dr. Anna Lembke’s role at a court session with Judge Polster. Dr. Lembke was giving testimony as an expert witness in support of plaintiffs in the opioid cases; she was not speaking solely as an addiction specialist.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Nov. 27, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-27T04:51:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/c63296eb-f5a1-5f64-8238-9191046de6ec', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c63296eb-f5a1-5f64-8238-9191046de6ec'}, {'abstract': 'The rate of births fell again last year, according to new government data, extending a lengthy decline as women wait until they are older to have children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/27/us/us-birth-fertility-rate.html', 'snippet': 'The rate of births fell again last year, according to new government data, extending a lengthy decline as women wait until they are older to have children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The fertility rate in the United States fell in 2018 for the fourth straight year, extending a steep decline in births that began in 2008 with the Great Recession, the federal government said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/us/26fertility/merlin_144659739_00863f4b-13ee-4ae3-8747-56d4b545c68d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 4