, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/world/27ambriefing-europe-promo/27ambriefing-europe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/27/world/27ambriefing-europe-promo/27ambriefing-europe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/world/27ambriefing-europe-promo/27ambriefing-europe2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Albania, Russia, Thanksgiving: Your Wednesday Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-11-27T05:13:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Ives', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ives', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a989b9-84ef-5c06-a60a-d7acf003a754', 'word_count': 1557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a989b9-84ef-5c06-a60a-d7acf003a754'}, {'abstract': 'Martin Scorsese’s acclaimed new gangster movie hits Netflix. And get Thanksgiving inspiration from “Julie & Julia,” which airs on Showtime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/27/arts/television/whats-on-tv-wednesday-the-irishman-and-julie-julia.html', 'snippet': 'Martin Scorsese’s acclaimed new gangster movie hits Netflix. And get Thanksgiving inspiration from “Julie & Julia,” which airs on Showtime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE IRISHMAN (2019) Stream on Netflix. “I don’t think 10 years ago, he makes a film like this,” Al Pacino said in a recent interview with The New York Times. The “he” there is Martin Scorsese, and the film is “The Irishman,” Scorsese’s new mob epic, which deals with made men, hits and betrayals, and with aging and legacy. Robert De Niro plays Frank Sheeran, a former hit man who tells the story of his life in organized crime. (He is based on a real person.) That story, seen in flashbacks that make up a large part of the movie, revolves around work for a Mafia figure played by Joe Pesci and, ultimately, and involves the disappearance of Jimmy Hoffa (played by Pacino). Bobby Cannavale, Anna Paquin and Ray Romano are in the film’s ensemble. “The movie is long and dark: long like a novel by Dostoyevsky or Dreiser, dark like a painting by Rembrandt,” A.O. Scott wrote in his review for The Times. “This is Scorsese’s least sentimental picture of mob life,” Scott added, “and for that reason his most poignant.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/arts/27tvcol-theirishman/27tvcol-theirishman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/arts/27tvcol-theirishman/27tvcol-theirishman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/arts/27tvcol-theirishman/27tvcol-theirishman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/arts/27tvcol-theirishman/27tvcol-theirishman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1102, 'width': 1651, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/arts/27tvcol-theirishman/27tvcol-t