eased on the round-number anniversary of its title? I can’t say. But here’s the math: Prince’s “1999,” the album that made him a rock star before “Purple Rain” made him a mass pop star, came out in 1982. That’s 37 years ago, though the music still sounds contemporary and alive. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 888}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1384, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/27princebox/27princebox-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Prince, More Pleasure: The Joys of the Expanded ‘1999’', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None