snippet': 'Six new paperbacks to check out this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE PARISIAN, by Isabella Hammad. (Grove, $18.) Set in France and Palestine from just before World War I to 1936, this novel sends its conflicted hero, a native of the ancient city of Nablus, to study in Paris, where he confronts European ways, eventually carrying some back home. Our reviewer, Christopher Benfey, described it as “exquisite,” with an “up-close immediacy.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/books/review/01Paperrow/01Paperrow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'wi