e industrial farms, small plots are rented out to field laborers so they can try to create their own farm businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALINAS, Calif. — The Salinas Valley is known for its enormous industrial farms that grow produce like lettuce and broccoli. But just southeast of the city of Salinas, a patchwork of much smaller organic fruit and vegetable fields breaks the industrial sprawl.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/opinion/26Fixes/26Fixes-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning Farm Workers Into Farmers', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant Labor (Agriculture)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Foods and Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Farmland Trust', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tufts University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michoacan (Mexico)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oaxaca (Mexico)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salinas (Calif)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-27T20:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Johnny Magdaleno', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Johnny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Magdaleno', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b09f2bdd-d525-590e-b899-0bc1b8cd8403', 'word_count': 1883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b09f2bdd-d525-590e-b899-0bc1b8cd8403'}, {'abstract': '“Lineup” spotlights the role of the stripe; Ann Greene Kelly’s recent drawings; Sérgio Sister’s prison art; Vanessa German’s power-figure sculptures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/27/arts/design/new-york-galleries-what-to-see-right-now.html', 'snippet': '“Lineup” spotlights the role of the stripe; Ann Greene Kelly’s recent drawings; Sérgio Sister’s prison art; Vanessa German’s power-figure sculptures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout Virginia Woolf’s “To the Lighthouse,” the painter Lily Briscoe struggles to complete a modern picture — and only on the final page, after painting a single stripe, does she wearily proclaim: “I have had my vision.” The 30 artists in “Lineup,” a show covering a century of art history and filled with more stripes than a jailhouse uniform shop, share with Woolf’s alter-ego painter a commitment to these linear bands, which structure a picture’s surface even as they shut down the illusion of three dimensions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1177, 'width': 1765, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/27galleries-lineup/27galleries-lineup-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Galleries: What to See Right Now', 'kicker': 'Art Reviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Galleries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lineup (Exhibit)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Almine Rech Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Ann Greene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chapter NY (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sister, Sergio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galeria Nara Roesler (Manhattan, NY, Gallery)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'German, Vanessa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fort Gansevoort (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-27T20:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebdbea97-fe78-5c79-8510-147ac660e150', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebdbea97-fe78-5c79-8510-147ac660e150'}, {'abstract': 'How much good does a preschool experience offer children born in poverty? Enough to make their later lives much better, and they pass a heritage of opportunity on to their own children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/27/opinion/how-to-break-the-poverty-cycle.html', 'snippet': 'How much good does a preschool experience offer children born in poverty? Enough to make their later lives much better, and they pass a heritage of opportunity on to their own children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1962, 58 African-American 3- and 4-year-olds, all from poor families and likely candidates for failure in school, enrolled in Perry Preschool in Ypsilanti, Mich. This was a novel venture, and parents clamored to sign their children up. Louise Derman-Sparks, who taught there, told me she “fell in love with the kids. They were so excited, so intelligent, so curious.” Because the demand could not be satisfied, 65 applicants were turned away. They became the control group in an experiment that confirmed the importance of a child’s first years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/opinion/27kirp1/merlin_147388782_e6198bc7-c1cb-4c81-94de-8e1bd0e4f3bb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/27/opinion/27kirp1/merlin_147388782_e6198bc7-c1cb-4c81-94de-8e1bd0e4f3bb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/27/opinion/27kirp1/merlin_147388782_e6198bc7-c1cb-4c81-94de-8e1bd0e4f3bb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/1