}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interscholastic Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-28T05:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bedford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bedford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e02a48b-d231-5946-b951-e48d5dd7fddc', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e02a48b-d231-5946-b951-e48d5dd7fddc'}, {'abstract': 'A psychological thriller series debuts on Apple TV Plus. And the first two “Godfather” movies air on IFC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday-servant-and-the-godfather-part-ii.html', 'snippet': 'A psychological thriller series debuts on Apple TV Plus. And the first two “Godfather” movies air on IFC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SERVANT Stream on Apple TV Plus. A recent trailer for this series has all the ingredients of a shocking story: an unsettling doll, foreboding rain and a title card that reads “from M. Night Shyamalan.” That filmmaker is an executive producer of the series, a psychological thriller about a couple (Lauren Ambrose and Toby Kebbell) who have lost a child. As part of a form of therapy meant to help them cope, the pair start taking care of a lifelike baby doll. They even enlist a nanny (Nell Tiger Free) to help — which is when matters begin to take a turn for the exceedingly strange.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/arts/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo/28tvcol-godfatherparttwo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday: ‘Servant’ and ‘The Godfather Part II’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-28T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabe Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32f79ba8-fd9b-5ed2-850b-ee69592084c2', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32f79ba8-fd9b-5ed2-850b-ee69592084c2'}, {'abstract': 'Arsenal Fan TV is a YouTube sensation. But what makes it a success is not the same thing as what makes Arsenal a success — in fact, it’s often the opposite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/28/sports/arsenal-fan-tv.html', 'snippet': 'Arsenal Fan TV is a YouTube sensation. But what makes it a success is not the same thing as what makes Arsenal a success — in fact, it’s often the opposite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Chris Davies walked out of the Emirates Stadium feeling, he said, as if he was “filled with fire.” As most of his fellow Arsenal fans trudged dolorously away from last Saturday’s 2-2 draw with lowly Southampton, seeking shelter in the pubs of the Holloway Road or the sanctuary of the Tube, he strode toward the statue of Dennis Bergkamp on the perimeter of the club’s North London home. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/sports/28soccerarsenaltv01/merlin_165111168_a75df61b-3af6-45be-9547-43001bc4d521-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/sports/28soccerarsenaltv01/merlin_165111168_a75df61b-3af6-45be-9547-43001bc4d521-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/sports/28soccerarsenaltv01/merlin_165111168_a75df61b-3af6-45be-9547-43001bc4d521-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '