 {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Kind Hearts and Coronets (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-28T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Hoberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5cae827-8c8f-5e5e-9090-13bd83a1ed72', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5cae827-8c8f-5e5e-9090-13bd83a1ed72'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer’s commitment to dance as a catalyst for social change can be seen at a museum show in Seattle and in a new work for the Alvin Ailey company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/28/arts/dance/donald-byrd-exhibition.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer’s commitment to dance as a catalyst for social change can be seen at a museum show in Seattle and in a new work for the Alvin Ailey company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — The choreographer Donald Byrd stood before a video of his younger self, observing a dance he created 33 years ago. In a button-down T-shirt, loose khaki pants and bare feet, the man onscreen floated through swift turns and bobbing leaps with the continuity of rushing water, letting the phrase resolve in a simple first position.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01DONALD-BYRD1/01DONALD-BYRD1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Dance Make a More Just America? Donald Byrd Is Working on It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Social Justice Movement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frye Art Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeFrantz, Thomas F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrd, Donald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spectrum Dance Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Greenwood (Dance)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The America That Is to Be (Exhibit)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-28T10:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd89d67a-ec94-51bc-a03a-e8a50deca0fe', 'word_count': 1521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd89d67a-ec94-51bc-a03a-e8a50deca0fe'}, {'abstract': 'There would be no herbs, or diffusers, or mysticism. There would be Oxycodone or Vicodin, and I would need to take it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/28/nyregion/opioids-prescription-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'There would be no herbs, or diffusers, or mysticism. There would be Oxycodone or Vicodin, and I would need to take it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon in early October I sat with a pain management specialist at the Hospital for Special Surgery, during a long day of orientation in advance of an operation that would replace the joint sockets and femoral heads on both my right and left hips, driving metal rods into my thigh bones. Reading about the procedure, I imagined something that happened in the service aisles at Home Depot, but with the addition of nerve endings.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/nyregion/01BIG/merlin_162873609_65f6b1e1-c148-4701-b461-fe06c1545be9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/nyregion/01BIG/merlin_162873609_65f6b1e1-c148-4701-b461-fe06c1545be9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u