8T10:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Reader Center', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45896246-7944-52aa-aac7-b26d7120ba68', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45896246-7944-52aa-aac7-b26d7120ba68'}, {'abstract': 'Prisoners who fought for years to prove their innocence couldn’t win in court, no matter how much evidence they amassed. Then the offices that put them away got involved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/28/us/conviction-integrity-unit-innocence.html', 'snippet': 'Prisoners who fought for years to prove their innocence couldn’t win in court, no matter how much evidence they amassed. Then the offices that put them away got involved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Aaron Salter was convicted of murdering a man he had never met, he immediately began trying to track down the real killer from behind bars. When another inmate described the crime in detail, Mr. Salter began investigating him. Eventually that other man signed an affidavit swearing that Mr. Salter was innocent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/28coldcase-01/merlin_165110937_4178bb5e-191d-4164-a285-7267a788cd0c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/28/us/28coldcase-01/merlin_165110937_4178bb5e-191d-4164-a285-7267a788cd0c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/28coldcase-01/merlin_165110937_4178bb5e-191d-4164-a285-7267a788cd0c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'ca