e of color, and they’re watching their country’s football team win the 2018 World Cup.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1127, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29lesmiserables/29lesmiserables-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Les Misérables’ Review: Injustice Still Stalks the Poor of Paris', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Injustice Stalks the Poor of Paris', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ly, Ladj', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Les Miserables (2019) (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-28T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7365ff59-bd48-5f4a-aeec-a0de6f4a6466', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7365ff59-bd48-5f4a-aeec-a0de6f4a6466'}, {'abstract': 'In this faux documentary, the relationship between an American filmmaker and her troubled immigrant subject takes on a darkly controlling hue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/28/movies/my-friend-the-polish-girl-review.html', 'snippet': 'In this faux documentary, the relationship between an American filmmaker and her troubled immigrant subject takes on a darkly controlling hue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Filmmakers who swing for the fences are inherently more interesting than those who play it safe. And no one can accuse Ewa Banaskiewicz and Mateusz Dymek, the writers and directors of “My Friend the Polish Girl,” of embracing safety in their singular, if somewhat forced attempt to query society’s callous treatment of immigrants.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/myfriend1/myfriend1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/myfriend1/myfriend1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't