ow his subjects, Andy Cohen paints a compelling portrait of those suffering from a public health crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An estimated 300,000 residents of Henan Province in China contracted H.I.V. during a local epidemic that dates to the 1990s, according to the documentary “Ximei.” At that time, officials encouraged peasants to sell their blood for pittances. The virus spread through contaminated equipment and transfusions. Years later, AIDS patients in Henan are still shunned — scorned by their families, denied care by certain hospitals and made to fill out complicated forms for reimbursement (even though many are illiterate).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29ximei-1/29ximei-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29ximei-1/29ximei-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29ximei-1/29ximei-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29ximei-1/29ximei-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1063, 'width': 1925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29ximei-1/29ximei-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/29/arts/29ximei-1/29ximei-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': Non