ia’s black farmworkers settled in waterless colonies. The history endures underground, through old pipes, dry wells and shoddy septic tanks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/29/us/water-racism-california.html', 'snippet': 'In the 20th century, California’s black farmworkers settled in waterless colonies. The history endures underground, through old pipes, dry wells and shoddy septic tanks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEVISTON, Calif. — Bertha Mae Beavers remembers hearing stories as a child about the promises of California, a place so rich with jobs and opportunity that money, she was told, “grew on trees.” So in the summer of 1946 she said goodbye to her family of sharecroppers in Oklahoma and set out for a piece of it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/merlin_164739135_1188deb7-7c81-4ec4-9c1d-f7b02ef1ad38-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/merlin_164739135_1188deb7-7c81-4ec4-9c1d-f7b02ef1ad38-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/merlin_164739135_1188deb7-7c81-4ec4-9c1d-f7b02ef1ad38-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/merlin_164739135_1188deb7-7c81-4ec4-9c1d-f7b02ef1ad38-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/00water-reparations2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/00water-reparations2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/20/us/00water-reparations2/00water-reparations2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Racism Ripples Through Rural California’s Pipes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dry Wells, Dirty Water and the Deep Roots of Segregation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Joaquin Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation and Desegregation', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-29T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jose A. Del Real', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jose', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Del', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba0eda1f-09d6-562d-baff-48a30f635cea', 'word_count': 1613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba0eda1f-09d6-562d-baff-48a30f635cea'}, {'abstract': 'Berluti’s Kris Van Assche shares the art — and fries shop — that inspires him the most.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/29/t-magazine/kris-van-assche-berluti.html', 'snippet': 'Berluti’s Kris Van Assche shares the art — and fries shop — that inspires him the most.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kris Van Assche, the artistic director of Berluti, grew up an only child in Belgium’s Flemish-speaking region of Londerzeel, between Antwerp and Brussels. “Nobody I knew was interested in art or fashion, so there was no predestination,” says the designer, 43. He credits his paternal grandmother with sparking his love of beauty, saying, “She always set a lovely table and she made all her own clothes — and mine.” After graduating from the Royal Academy of Fine Arts Antwerp, where he studied women’s wear, in 1998, Van Assche was offered an internship designing men’s wear for Yves Saint Laurent; unsure if he wanted to live in Paris, he decided it would be a good placeholder until he found other work in London, Milan or New York. But then he met Hedi Slimane, at the time the brand’s creative director of men’s wear, whom he followed to Dior Homme in 2000. Four years later, Van Assche started his own label — conceptual suiting with a sportswear bent — only to return to Dior in 2007 to replace Slimane in the top job.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '78', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 751}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 818, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1636, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/t-magazine/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V/08tmag-profile-slide-D13V-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Men’s Wear Designer Keeping a Heritage Brand Cool', 'kicker': 'Profile in Style', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kris Van Assche', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berluti', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dior Homme (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Assche, Kris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTWERP (BELGIUM)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rosas Danst Rosas (Dance)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-29T10:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalia Rachlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rachlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5c36d8c-7c14-579b-a1fb-bb090ec7c157', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5c36d8c-7c14-579b-a1fb-bb090ec7c157'}, {'abstract': 'Savannah, Ga., is a pilgrimage destination for those interested in the abolitionist’s life, with artists interpreting his legacy in riveting shows and a film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/29/arts/design/frederick-douglass-savannah.html', 'snippet': 'Savannah, Ga., is a pilgrimage destination for those interested in the abolitionist’s life, with artists interpreting his legacy in riveting shows and a film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAVANNAH, Ga. — Frederick Douglass passed through this elegant Southern city only once, for the briefest of visits — a half-hour whistle-stop on his rail journey to a speaking engagement in Jacksonville, Fla.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01savannah-art1/01savannah-art1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/arts/01savannah-art1/01savannah-art1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheig