anization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e423931-7d64-5c48-94f4-2fa12eef2e79', 'word_count': 2146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e423931-7d64-5c48-94f4-2fa12eef2e79'}, {'abstract': 'Watch as artisans deftly construct a luxury timepiece, from the ceramic band to the steel-edged case to the self-winding internal mechanism, at the brand’s atelier in Switzerland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/t-magazine/100000006834800/t-process-chanel-j12-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Watch as artisans deftly construct a luxury timepiece, from the ceramic band to the steel-edged case to the self-winding internal mechanism, at the brand’s atelier in Switzerland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watch as artisans deftly construct a luxury timepiece, from the ceramic band to the steel-edged case to the self-winding internal mechanism, at the brand’s atelier in Switzerland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch/25tmag-chanel-watch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'T Process | Chanel J12 Watch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-29T16:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gautier Billotte', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gautier', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Billotte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/35c26093-7335-538c-b79c-c0079cd0bc3e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/35c26093-7335-538c-b79c-c0079cd0bc3e'}, {'abstract': 'Each of the Parisian house’s iconic J12 watches is crafted by hand at the brand’s atelier in Switzerland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/29/t-magazine/chanel-j12-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Each of the Parisian house’s iconic J12 watches is crafted by hand at the brand’s atelier in Switzerland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Chanel released the J12 watch in 2000, it rocked the buttoned-up world of luxury timepieces. Conceived by the house’s then artistic director, Jacques Helleu, the design was cast in matte monochromatic ceramic, a material that gave the women’s accessory a fresh, graphic athleticism. “There was such authority to the design that you either loved it or hated it, but you could not be indifferent,” recalls Arnaud Chastaingt, who became the director of the Chanel Watch Creation Studio in 2013, following a 10-year tenure as a designer at Cartier. “The best creations work that way. That’s a sign of success for me.” Available first in jet black, and later in white, the J12 combines the functionality of a sports watch with the elegance of a link bracelet style. It proved wildly popular and has since joined the N°5 fragrance and the 2.55 handbag as one of Chanel’s most iconic creations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/25/t-magazine/25tmag-chanel-watch02/25tmag-chanel-watch02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It Takes Two Months to Make This Classic Chanel Timepiece', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-29T16:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Cavanagh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavanagh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f15418ca-b099-5afc-8abc-476ae77ee806', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f15418ca-b099-5afc-8abc-476ae77ee806'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibition in New York showcases the boundary-pushing, but long overlooked, work of Zilia Sánchez.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/29/t-magazine/zilia-sanchez.html', 'snippet': 'A new exhibition in New York showcases the boundary-pushing, but long overlooked, work of Zilia Sánchez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Delicate jet-black brush strokes pattern the pastel surfaces of Zilia Sánchez’s work like tattoos on human skin. The canvases themselves seem to contract and expand, as if breathing. Beneath the surface, invisible to the viewer’s eye, are wooden skeletons that give these works their wondrous three-dimensionality, transforming paintings into sculptures that resemble bent elbows, erect nipples and pointed tongues and suggest existential explorations of space. Since the 1950s, Sánchez, who is now 93, has dared to expand the dimensional constraints of painting with boundless ingenuity, conceiving a new visual language for sensuality. But unlike other artists who warped canvases to provocative effect, like the American sculptor Lee Bontecou and the Argentine-Italian painter Lucio Fontana, Sánchez worked for decades in obscurity.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/26/t-magazine/fashion/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6/zilla-sanchez-slide-DZD6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Who Transforms Paintings Into Cosmic Sculptures', 'kicker': 'Artist’s Questionnaire', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coming Into View', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Maria (2017)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Museo del Barrio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-29T16:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Furman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bf8d7a7-0662-5fdc-847b-3336879151d7', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bf8d7a7-0662-5fdc-847b-3336879151d7'}, {'abstract': 'Most Americans view President Trump’s potential impeachment along partisan lines. But a crucial slice of the electorate remains undecided, with possible implications for the 2020 election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/29/us/politics/impeachment-trump-polls.html', 'snippet': 'Most Americans view President Trump’s potential impeachment along partisan lines. But a crucial slice of the electorate remains undecided, with possible implications for the 2020 election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Poll Watch, our weekly look at polling data and survey research on the candidates, voters and issues that will shape the 2020 election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The N