n_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tish Harrison Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tish', 'middlename': 'Harrison', 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/07b4b303-9a05-5a07-b43a-de8b1bdf3257', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07b4b303-9a05-5a07-b43a-de8b1bdf3257'}, {'abstract': 'Nature did for me what yoga, psychedelics and therapy couldn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/30/sunday-review/cloud-forest-ferns.html', 'snippet': 'Nature did for me what yoga, psychedelics and therapy couldn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I liked Oaxaca as soon as I learned to say its name, all those airy vowels, each subsequent “a” a little fuller in my mouth. Last year, I was in the throes of a deep depression. But reading “Oaxaca Journal,” Oliver Sacks’s account of traveling that Mexican state to study its flora with the New York Fern Society, made me feel dreamy and brave. A flash of wanderlust, my fascination with the fern (which began when I failed at keeping one alive in my tiny Brooklyn studio) and a physical urge to escape the brutal careerism of New York all nudged me into opening my laptop, taking a chance on my savings and booking a one-way ticket to the region.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/merlin_158448492_7255a71a-8a96-40c5-a6f2-f0f56b13d4bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/merlin_158448492_7255a71a-8a96-40c5-a6f2-f0f56b13d4bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/merlin_158448492_7255a71a-8a96-40c5-a6f2-f0f56b13d4bc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/merlin_158448492_7255a71a-8a96-40c5-a6f2-f0f56b13d4bc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1410, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/18tchou1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/18tchou1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/18tchou1/18tchou1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Malaise, Cured by a Cloud Forest?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Malaise, Cured by Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eco-Tourism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oaxaca (Mexico)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-11-30T19:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wei Tchou', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tchou', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/39d98157-6b71-508c-8fb3-87fcd986d47c', 'word_count': 1503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39d98157-6b71-508c-8fb3-87fcd986d47c'}, {'abstract': 'My 2019 holiday guide has some great causes. And one is already promised $100,000 from a reader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/30/opinion/sunday/holiday-gift-guide.html', 'snippet': 'My 2019 holiday guide has some great causes. And one is already promised $100,000 from a reader.', 'lead_paragraph': '’Tis the season for giving, when those of us in the rich world hand each other overpriced scarves that no one much wants.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/opinion/01kristofA-03/01kristofA-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/opinion/01kristofA-03/01kristofA-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/opinion/01kristofA-03/01kristofA-03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/opinion/01kristofA-03/01kristofA-03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/opinion/01kristofA-03/01kristofA-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/